      "name": "InitializeBinkFileHandle",
      "signature": "DWORD InitializeBinkFileHandle(BinkFileHandle * pFileHandle, LPCSTR lpszFilePath, UINT dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "DWORD",
      "comment": "Initializes a Bink file handle structure with function pointers and file access.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Zero-initialize the entire BinkFileHandle structure (200 bytes)\n2. Check BINK_DIRECT_HANDLE flag (0x800000) in dwFlags parameter\n3. If direct handle mode: Store handle directly and get file size via SetFilePointer\n4. If normal file mode: Open file with CreateFileA, retry with different share flags if needed\n5. Populate function pointer table with Bink I/O operations\n6. Return success (1) or failure (0) based on file handle validity\n\nParameters:\npFileHandle - Pointer to BinkFileHandle structure to initialize (200 bytes)\nlpszFilePath - File path string for normal mode, or file handle cast to string for direct mode  \ndwFlags - Bink flags, bit 0x800000 indicates direct handle mode\nIMPLICIT - None\n\nReturns:\n1 (TRUE) - Success, file handle initialized and function pointers set\n0 (FALSE) - Failure, could not open file in normal mode\n\nSpecial Cases:\nCreateFileA called twice with different sharing flags (FILE_SHARE_READ=1, then FILE_SHARE_READ|FILE_SHARE_WRITE=3)\nDirect mode treats lpszFilePath parameter as HANDLE cast to string\nMagic number 0x32 (50 decimal) = structure size in DWORDs (200 bytes / 4)\n\nStructure Layout BinkFileHandle:\nOffset  Size  Field Name      Type     Description\n0x00    4     pfnRead         void*    Read function pointer  \n0x04    4     pfnWrite        void*    Write function pointer\n0x08    4     pfnSeek         void*    Seek function pointer\n0x0c    4     pfnTell         void*    Tell function pointer  \n0x10    4     pfnClose        void*    Close function pointer\n0x14    4     pfnGetSize      void*    GetSize function pointer\n0x18    60    reserved1       uint[15] Reserved space\n0x48    4     hFile           HANDLE   File handle\n0x4c    36    reserved2       uint[9]  Reserved space  \n0x70    4     bDirectHandle   uint     Direct handle flag\n0x74    4     dwFileSize      uint     File size in bytes\n\nFlag Bits dwFlags:\n0x800000 - BINK_DIRECT_HANDLE: Use lpszFilePath as direct file handle",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
