      "name": "BinkFileTell",
      "signature": "void BinkFileTell(BinkFileHandle * pFileHandle, int nPosition, uint dwFlags, uint dwUserData1, uint dwUserData2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets Bink file position and configures file handle parameters for streaming operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment thread-safe lock counter at pFileHandle+0x5c using LOCK prefix\n2. Wait for any pending operations by checking busy flag at pFileHandle+0x60\n3. While busy flag is non-zero, yield CPU time and call BinkService to process pending requests\n4. Extract page-aligned address from dwFlags by masking upper 20 bits (0xfffff000)\n5. Store nPosition to multiple file handle offsets: +0x64, +0x54, +0x6c for position tracking\n6. Calculate and store end position (nPosition + masked flags) at +0x68\n7. Store page-aligned base addresses at +0x38 and +0x58 for memory mapping\n8. Clear seek offset flag at +0x44 to indicate new position\n9. Store user data parameters at +0x78 and +0x7c for caller-specific context\n10. Decrement lock counter using LOCK prefix to release critical section\n\nParameters:\npFileHandle (BinkFileHandle *): File handle structure containing stream state and position information\nnPosition (int): New file position in bytes from start of file\ndwFlags (uint): Configuration flags where upper 20 bits specify page-aligned memory base address\ndwUserData1 (uint): User-defined data stored in file handle for caller context\ndwUserData2 (uint): Additional user-defined data stored in file handle\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function blocks if BinkService is busy processing other requests\n- Page alignment ensures dwFlags upper 20 bits (0xfffff000) represent 4KB-aligned addresses\n- Multiple position fields suggest redundant storage for different subsystems\n- Lock mechanism prevents race conditions during multi-threaded file operations\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x5c (92): Offset to thread-safe lock counter byte\n0x60 (96): Offset to busy flag indicating pending operations  \n0x18 (24): Offset to BinkService context pointer\n0x64 (100): Primary position storage offset\n0x54 (84): Secondary position storage offset  \n0x6c (108): Tertiary position storage offset\n0x68 (104): End position storage (nPosition + page-aligned base)\n0x38 (56): Page-aligned base address storage\n0x58 (88): Duplicate page-aligned base address storage\n0x44 (68): Seek offset flag cleared to indicate position change\n0x78 (120): User data 1 storage offset\n0x7c (124): User data 2 storage offset\n0xfffff000: Page alignment mask for 4KB boundaries",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
