      "name": "ExpandPlane",
      "signature": "uint * ExpandPlane(uint * pDestBuffer, uint * pSourcePlane, uint dwPlaneWidth, uint dwPlaneHeight, uint dwDestStride, uint * pSourceBuffer, uint dwFlags, int nMaskBuffer, uint dwPixelStep, uint * ppHuffmanTrees, uint dwBinkFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint *",
      "comment": "Expands a video plane using Bink video codec decompression with block-based processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize Huffman decoder trees for motion vectors, DCT coefficients, and color data\n2. Calculate blocks per row and destination stride differences for plane geometry\n3. Select DCT function pointer based on Bink flags (0x8000 determines standard vs alternative)\n4. Initialize all decoder streams using FUN_10003be0 with 0x200 element arrays\n5. Process initial decoder state for motion vectors, coefficients, and color tables\n6. For each row of blocks in the plane:\n   a. Update decoder states for current row using FUN_10004250/FUN_10004cc0/etc\n   b. For each block in the row, decode block type from stream\n   c. Process block based on type (0-9):\n      - Type 0: Copy 8x8 block directly from source to destination\n      - Type 1: Decode using motion vector compensation with sub-block processing\n      - Type 2: Motion compensation using horizontal/vertical offset tables\n      - Type 3: DCT coefficient decoding with run-length and quantization\n      - Type 4: Copy 8x8 source block then apply 7-bit differential encoding\n      - Type 5: DCT reconstruction using InverseDiscreteCosineTransformWithTableIndex\n      - Type 6: Fill 8x8 block with solid color value from coefficient stream\n      - Type 7: Complex DCT with motion compensation and PerformIdct2d8x8\n      - Type 8: 4-color palette mode using 2-bit indices per pixel\n      - Type 9: Direct 16-pixel block copy from coefficient stream\n7. Advance row pointers by destination stride and update mask buffer offset\n8. Continue until all plane rows processed\n\nParameters:\npDestBuffer - Output buffer for decompressed plane data\npSourcePlane - Source plane buffer containing reference data\nnPlaneWidth - Width of plane in pixels (must be multiple of 8)\nnPlaneHeight - Height of plane in pixels (must be multiple of 8) \nnDestStride - Destination buffer stride in bytes per row\npSourceBuffer - Additional source buffer for motion compensation\ndwFlags - Codec flags controlling DCT function selection\npMaskBuffer - Bit mask buffer for tracking processed blocks\nnPixelStep - Pixel step size for interleaved formats\nppHuffmanTrees - Array of 9 Huffman decoder trees for different data types\ndwBinkFlags - Bink codec flags (bit 0x8000 selects DCT variant)\n\nReturns:\nPointer to current position in bitstream after plane processing\n\nSpecial Cases:\nBlock types 1,3-9: Set mask bit indicating block processing\nType 1 sub-cases: 3,5,6,8,9 have distinct coefficient/color processing\nBit accumulator: Handles variable-length codes with 32-bit window\nDCT tables: 64-element coefficient arrays for 8x8 transform blocks\nColor palette: 4-entry lookup for 2-bit indexed color mode\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x8000 - DCT function selection flag in dwBinkFlags\n0x200 - Huffman tree array size (512 elements)\n0x3f - Maximum run-length index for DCT coefficient tables\n0x7f - 7-bit mask for differential encoding mode\n0xf - 4-bit mask for color indices and coefficient selection\n0x1f - 31-bit right shift for bit accumulator management",
