      "name": "DecodeHuffmanSymbols",
      "signature": "void DecodeHuffmanSymbols(BitStream * pBitStream, uint * pdwLengthTable, uint * pdwSymbolCount, byte * pbSymbolBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Decodes Huffman-encoded symbols from a bit stream into symbol buffer.\n\nThis function implements a multi-level Huffman decoder for compressed data streams.\nIt extracts variable-length codes and maps them to symbols using lookup tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract 4-bit symbol index from bit stream\n2. Look up base pointer and count in global tables (PTR_DAT_1002a030, DAT_100279c8)\n3. Store length table pointer and symbol count in output parameters\n4. If symbol index is 0: Fill buffer with sequential values (0-15)\n5. If symbol index is non-zero: Perform hierarchical symbol decoding\n   a. Read 1-bit flag to determine decoding path (simple vs complex)\n   b. For simple path (flag=0): Read 2-bit sub-index for direct symbol pairs\n   c. For complex path (flag=1): Read 3-bit length, then decode symbols sequentially\n6. Update bit stream state with new position and remaining bits\n\nParameters:\npBitStream - Pointer to BitStream structure containing data pointer and bit position\npdwLengthTable - Output pointer to receive address of length table for symbol set\npdwSymbolCount - Output pointer to receive count of symbols in current set\npbSymbolBuffer - Output buffer to receive decoded 16-byte symbol sequence\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nSymbol index 0: Direct sequential fill (symbols 0-15)\nSymbol index 1-15: Hierarchical decoding using global lookup tables\n\nStructure Layout:\nBitStream (16 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type      Description\n0x00    4     pData            uint*     Pointer to current data position\n0x04    4     nOffset          int       Byte offset in stream\n0x08    4     dwBitBuffer      uint      Current 32-bit bit buffer\n0x0C    4     nBitsAvailable   uint      Number of valid bits in buffer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1002a030 - Global pointer table for length data addresses\n0x100279c8 - Global byte table containing symbol counts per index\n0x4 (4) - Number of bits for initial symbol index extraction\n0x10 (16) - Fixed size of output symbol buffer\n0x1F (31) - Mask for 32-bit word boundary (bits 0-31)\n0x1C (28) - Bit count adjustment for word loading (32-4)\n0x1E (30) - Bit count adjustment for 2-bit extraction (32-2)\n0x1D (29) - Bit count adjustment for 3-bit extraction (32-3)\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error handling - assumes valid bit stream input\nCaller responsible for ensuring sufficient data in stream\nBuffer overrun protection via fixed 16-byte output limit",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
