      "name": "ProcessHuffmanBlock",
      "signature": "void ProcessHuffmanBlock(HuffmanDecodeContext * pDecompressContext, BitStream * pBitStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Process a single Huffman-compressed data block using decompression context and bit stream.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate decompression buffer state (empty buffer condition check)\n2. Extract bit count mask and read block size from Huffman decode context\n3. Initialize bit stream pointers and remaining bit counters\n4. Calculate bit alignment and extract compressed data size\n5. Handle special case: zero-length block (advance pointers by 4 bytes)\n6. For non-zero blocks, set up output buffer pointers and boundaries\n7. Check bit availability and load next data word if needed\n8. Test compression type flag in bit buffer (bit 0)\n9. Branch A - Huffman compression (flag = 0):\n   a. Load table bit width from decode context\n   b. Initialize symbol counter and last symbol cache\n   c. Loop until all bytes decoded:\n      - Extract table index using bit mask and table lookup\n      - Fetch symbol and bit count from decode tables\n      - Update bit buffer and remaining bit counter\n      - If symbol < 0x0C: write literal byte, update last symbol\n      - If symbol >= 0x0C: perform run-length expansion using last symbol\n10. Branch B - Literal compression (flag = 1):\n    a. Extract 4-bit nibble from bit buffer\n    b. Replicate nibble pattern across output buffer\n    c. Handle both 4-byte aligned writes and remaining byte writes\n11. Update bit stream state with final pointers and bit counts\n\nParameters:\npDecompressContext - Pointer to HuffmanDecodeContext containing decode tables and buffer state\npBitStream - Pointer to BitStream containing input data pointer and bit state\n\nReturns:\nvoid (function updates structures in-place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEmpty buffer condition (*pDecompressContext == pDecompressContext[1]) returns immediately\nZero-length block advances buffer pointers by 4 bytes without decompression\nLiteral mode replicates 4-bit values across entire output buffer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x0C (12) - Threshold between literal symbols and run-length codes\n0x20 (32) - Bit width for DWORD operations and bit mask calculations\n0x1F (31) - Bit count mask for shift operations\n0xFFFFFFFF - Full bit mask for bit extraction operations\n0x0F0F0F0F - Nibble replication mask for literal mode\n0x100279CC - Global array g_abHuffmanSymbolCounts base address\n\nStructure Layout - HuffmanDecodeContext:\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type    Description\n0x00    4     nOutputStart        int     Output buffer start pointer\n0x04    4     nOutputEnd          int     Output buffer end pointer  \n0x20    1     bTableBitWidth      byte    Huffman table bit width\n0x24    4     pLookupTable        int     Symbol lookup table pointer\n0x28    4     dwBitCountMask      uint    Bit extraction mask\n0x2C    4     pOutputBuffer       int     Current output buffer pointer\n\nStructure Layout - BitStream:\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type    Description\n0x00    4     pInputData          uint*   Input data pointer\n0x04    4     nSavedState         int     Saved stream state\n0x08    4     dwBitBuffer         uint    Current bit buffer\n0x0C    4     dwRemainingBits     uint    Remaining bits in buffer\n\nFlag Bits:\nBit 0 (0x01) - Compression type: 0=Huffman coded, 1=Literal/nibble mode",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
