      "name": "DecodeHuffmanStream",
      "signature": "void DecodeHuffmanStream(int * pDecoderState, int * pBitReader, int * pDecodeTable)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Decodes a Huffman-compressed bitstream into output bytes using symbol lookup tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate decoder state - check if output buffer has space (start != end)\n2. Initialize bit reader state - extract current word pointer, bit buffer, and available bits\n3. Determine bit extraction method based on available bits vs required bits\n4. Extract symbol length bits from decode table at offset 0x100 + symbol*4\n5. Use symbol length to mask bits and lookup symbol in table at offset 0x140 + symbol*4  \n6. Decode symbol into high/low nibbles using symbol & 0xf and symbol >> 4\n7. Extract distance length bits from decoder state offset 0x20 (8 bits)\n8. Use distance length to lookup distance value from state offset 0x24\n9. Combine symbol high nibble (shifted left 4) with distance low nibble\n10. Store combined byte to output buffer and advance output pointer\n11. Decrement bytes remaining counter and repeat until complete\n12. Handle buffer underrun - fill remaining bytes with repeated first output byte\n13. Update decode table current symbol at offset 0x180\n14. Restore bit reader state with final word pointer and bit counts\n\nParameters:\npDecoderState - Pointer to decoder state structure containing output buffer pointers and bit extraction state\npBitReader - Pointer to bit reader state with current stream position and bit buffer\npDecodeTable - Pointer to decode table structure with symbol lookup tables at offsets 0x100, 0x140, 0x180\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates decoder state and bit reader state in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf output buffer is empty (start == end), function exits early without decoding\nIf decoded length exceeds available output space, fills remainder with first decoded byte\nDirection bit (bit 0 of first extracted bits) controls length calculation: 0 = normal, 1 = subtract 0x14\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x100 - Offset to symbol length lookup table in decode structure  \n0x140 - Offset to symbol value lookup table in decode structure\n0x180 - Offset to current symbol storage in decode structure\n0x20 - Bit count for distance symbol extraction (32 bits)\n0x1f - Mask for 5-bit shift amounts (31 decimal)\n0x14 - Adjustment value (20 decimal) subtracted when direction bit is set\n0x16 - Minimum buffer underrun threshold (-22 decimal) for fill operation\n\nStructure Layout:\nDecoderState (48 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type    Description\n0x00    4     pOutputStart      uint    Start of output buffer  \n0x04    4     pOutputEnd        uint    End of output buffer\n0x08-0x24 28   dwReserved1-7     uint    Reserved fields\n0x28    4     dwBitCount        uint    Number of bits to extract\n0x2c    4     pOutputBuffer     uint    Current output buffer pointer\n\nBitReader (16 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type    Description  \n0x00    4     pCurrentWord      uint    Pointer to current 32-bit word in stream\n0x04    4     dwStreamPos       uint    Current position in stream\n0x08    4     dwBitBuffer       uint    Current bit buffer value\n0x0c    4     dwBitsAvailable   uint    Number of valid bits in buffer\n\nDecodeTable (772 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type    Description\n0x00    256   abLookupTable     byte[256]  Symbol lookup table\n0x100   256   adLengthTable     uint[64]   Symbol length table  \n0x140   256   apSymbolTable     uint[64]   Symbol value table\n0x180   4     dwCurrentSymbol   uint       Current symbol index",
