      "name": "DecompressBitstreamData",
      "signature": "void DecompressBitstreamData(BitstreamContext * pContext, BitStream * pBitStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Decompresses encoded data from a bitstream using Huffman-style lookup tables\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify decoder context has available buffer space (*param_1 == param_1[1])\n2. Initialize local state from bitstream (data pointer, accumulator, bit position)\n3. Extract initial symbol bits from current bitstream position using param_1[10] bit width\n4. Calculate bit mask and perform bit shifting based on available bits vs required bits\n5. Set output buffer pointer from param_1[0xb] (output buffer base)\n6. If no bytes to decode (local_14 == 0), set buffer pointers for empty decode\n7. Enter main decoding loop for each byte to decompress:\n   a. Load symbol from lookup table at param_1[9] using masked bit accumulator\n   b. Extract low nibble using (symbol & 0xf) + 0x10 + param_1 offset\n   c. Extract high nibble from (symbol >> 4) bit count\n   d. Advance bit position and update accumulator with consumed bits\n   e. Repeat for second nibble of same output byte\n   f. Combine nibbles: (high << 4) | low and store to output buffer\n   g. Advance output pointer and decrement remaining byte count\n8. Update bitstream state with final position and accumulator values\n\nParameters:\n  param_1 (int *) - Decoder context structure containing:\n    [0]:   Current output buffer write pointer  \n    [1]:   Output buffer end pointer\n    [8]:   Lookup table bit width mask\n    [9]:   Symbol lookup table base pointer\n    [10]:  Initial symbol bit width (typically 4-8 bits)\n    [11]:  Output buffer base pointer for this decode operation\n    [16+]: Symbol-to-nibble translation table (16 byte offset)\n  param_2 (int *) - Bitstream state structure containing:\n    [0]:   Input data pointer (auto-advanced)\n    [1]:   Saved state value (preserved across call) \n    [2]:   Current bit accumulator (32-bit buffer)\n    [3]:   Current bit position within accumulator\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function updates structures in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early return if no output buffer space available (*param_1 == param_1[1])\n  - Zero-length decode updates buffer pointers but skips main loop\n  - Bit accumulator automatically refills from input stream when exhausted\n  - Symbol lookup uses two-stage process: table index then nibble translation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x1f (31)     - Bit mask for shift count modulo 32\n  0x20 (32)     - Bits per accumulator word\n  0xffffffff    - Full 32-bit mask for bit field extraction\n  0xf (15)      - Low nibble mask for symbol extraction  \n  0x10 (16)     - Offset to nibble translation table in context\n  4             - Bit shift for high nibble extraction\n\nStructure Layout - Decoder Context (param_1):\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type     Description\n0x00    4     pOutputCurrent       int *    Current write position\n0x04    4     pOutputEnd          int *    End of output buffer  \n0x20    4     dwLookupBitMask     int      Lookup table bit width\n0x24    4     pSymbolTable        int      Symbol lookup table base\n0x28    4     dwInitialBitWidth   int      Initial symbol bit count\n0x2C    4     pOutputBase         int      Base of current output buffer\n0x40    16    abNibbleTable       byte[16] Symbol to nibble translation\n\nStructure Layout - Bitstream State (param_2):\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type     Description  \n0x00    4     pInputData          int *    Current input position\n0x04    4     nSavedState         int      Preserved state value\n0x08    4     dwAccumulator       int      32-bit accumulator  \n0x0C    4     dwBitPosition       int      Current bit offset\n\nNote: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary variable optimized away by decompiler",
