      "name": "ExpandBinkPlanes",
      "signature": "void ExpandBinkPlanes(uint * pYPlaneTarget, uint * pYPlaneSource, uint * pUPlaneTarget, uint * pVPlaneTarget, int nBinkDataHandler, int nPlaneWidth, int nPlaneHeight, uint dwStride, uint dwVideoHeight, uint * pDataBuffer, uint dwCompressionFlags, uint * pFrameBuffer, uint dwProcessFlags, uint dwVideoFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Expands and processes Bink video frame data for Y, U, and V color planes\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if alpha channel processing is enabled (dwVideoFlags & 0x100000)\n   - If UV processing enabled (dwProcessFlags & 0x100000): Call ExpandPlane for UV data\n   - Otherwise: Simple buffer advance by reading buffer size\n2. Check buffer stride flag (dwProcessFlags & 0x8000)\n   - If clear: Advance data buffer pointer by 4 bytes\n3. Expand Y (luminance) plane using ExpandPlane function\n   - Width and height are 8-byte aligned ((value + 7) & 0xfffffff8)\n   - Single component processing (component = 1)\n4. Handle buffer pointer adjustment for Y plane\n   - If stride flag clear: Adjust based on previous buffer size minus 4 bytes\n5. Process UV (chrominance) planes if flag not set (!(dwProcessFlags & 0x20000))\n   - Calculate UV plane starting addresses: Y plane base + stride * height\n   - Halve dimensions for UV processing ((dimension + 1) >> 1)\n   - Call ExpandPlane twice for U and V planes (component = 2)\n\nParameters:\npYPlaneTarget    - Target buffer for Y (luminance) plane data\npYPlaneSource    - Source buffer for Y plane data  \npUPlaneTarget    - Target buffer for U (chroma) plane data\npVPlaneTarget    - Target buffer for V (chroma) plane data\nnBinkDataHandler - Bink codec data handler/context\nnPlaneWidth      - Width of video plane in pixels\nnPlaneHeight     - Height of video plane in pixels\ndwStride         - Byte stride between rows in target buffer\ndwVideoHeight    - Total video frame height\npDataBuffer      - Current position in compressed data buffer\ndwCompressionFlags - Compression method flags\npFrameBuffer     - Frame decoding buffer pointer\ndwProcessFlags   - Processing control flags\ndwVideoFlags     - Video format and feature flags\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nProcessing flags control data flow and plane handling\nUV planes are processed at half resolution (subsampled)\nBuffer pointers are advanced based on embedded size values\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x100000 (1048576) - Alpha/UV processing enable flag\n0x8000 (32768)     - Buffer stride handling flag  \n0x20000 (131072)   - UV plane processing skip flag\n0xfffffff8         - 8-byte alignment mask (clears low 3 bits)\n7                  - Alignment padding constant\n1                  - Y plane component identifier\n2                  - UV plane component identifier",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
