      "name": "ExtractMaskedBits",
      "signature": "uint ExtractMaskedBits(uint dwSourceFlags, uint dwMask)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Extracts bits from source value using a bitmask filter.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Initialize dwResult to 0, bit masks to 1, and counter to 32 (0x20)\n2. For each bit position (32 iterations):\n   a. Check if current bit is set in dwMask (dwMask & dwBitMask != 0)\n   b. If mask bit is set, check corresponding bit in dwSourceFlags\n   c. If source bit is also set, include this bit in result (dwResult |= dwBitMask)\n   d. If mask bit was set, advance source bit mask (dwSourceBitMask <<= 1)\n   e. Always advance mask bit position (dwBitMask <<= 1)\n   f. Decrement counter and continue until all 32 bits processed\n3. Return the extracted result containing only bits where mask was set\n\nParameters:\n\ndwSourceFlags - uint: Source value containing bits to extract\ndwMask - uint: Bitmask specifying which bits to examine/extract\n\nReturns:\n\nuint: Extracted bits where dwMask bits were set, positioned at original bit locations\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nIf dwMask is 0, function returns 0 (no bits to extract)\nIf dwSourceFlags is 0, function returns 0 (no source bits set)\nFunction processes all 32 bits regardless of input values\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x1 - Initial bit mask value (bit 0)\n0x20 - Loop counter for 32-bit processing (32 decimal)\n\nError Handling:\n\nNo error conditions - function always completes successfully\nHandles all possible uint input values without validation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:8d037910f675db1b341455807d56a33e",
