      "name": "BinkRestoreCursor",
      "signature": "void BinkRestoreCursor(int nCursorHideCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Restores cursor visibility by calling ShowCursor multiple times to undo hide operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if hide count parameter is non-zero\n2. Loop through hide count, decrementing each iteration  \n3. Call ShowCursor(1) once per iteration to increment cursor display counter\n4. Continue until count reaches zero\n5. Return when cursor fully restored\n\nParameters:\nnCursorHideCount (int): Number of ShowCursor(1) calls needed to restore cursor visibility.\n                       Corresponds to number of times cursor was previously hidden.\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Function modifies system cursor state directly.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nCursorHideCount is 0, function returns immediately without calls\n- ShowCursor(1) increments Windows internal cursor display counter\n- Each ShowCursor(0) call requires matching ShowCursor(1) to restore visibility\n\nError Handling:\n- No explicit error handling - relies on ShowCursor API robustness\n- Zero or negative counts handled by conditional check and loop structure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "EXP",
      "index": "EXP:39",
