      "name": "BinkBufferCheckWindowPosition",
      "signature": "void BinkBufferCheckWindowPosition(BinkBuffer * pBuffer, int * pnWidth, int * pnHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Adjusts Bink video buffer dimensions to fit within screen bounds with proper alignment.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate buffer pointer is not NULL, return early if NULL\n2. Process width dimension if pnWidth parameter provided:\n   a. Calculate total width: requested width + buffer X offset (pBuffer[7])\n   b. If clipping enabled (pBuffer[0x20] != 0), clamp to screen bounds:\n      - If total exceeds screen width, reduce to fit: width = screenWidth - bufferX\n      - If result is negative, set to zero\n   c. Apply video memory alignment based on g_dwVideoMemory:\n      - Mode 4 (16-bit): Align to 2-byte boundary (add 1, mask 0xFFFFFFFE)\n      - Mode 3 (24-bit): Align to 8-byte boundary (add 7, mask 0xFFFFFFF8)  \n      - Other modes: Align to 4-byte boundary (add 3, mask 0xFFFFFFFC)\n   d. Store final aligned width: *pnWidth = aligned_width - buffer_X_offset\n3. Process height dimension if pnHeight parameter provided:\n   a. Calculate total height: requested height + buffer Y offset (pBuffer[8])\n   b. If clipping enabled (pBuffer[0x20] != 0), clamp to screen bounds:\n      - If total exceeds screen height, reduce to fit: height = screenHeight - bufferY\n      - If result is negative, set to zero\n   c. Store final height: *pnHeight = adjusted_height - buffer_Y_offset\n\nParameters:\npBuffer - Pointer to BinkBuffer structure containing position and clipping settings\npnWidth - Pointer to width value to be adjusted (optional, can be NULL)  \npnHeight - Pointer to height value to be adjusted (optional, can be NULL)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Adjustments are made in-place through pointer parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL buffer pointer: Function returns immediately without processing\n- NULL width/height pointers: Corresponding dimension is skipped\n- Negative dimensions after clamping: Set to zero to prevent underflow\n- Video memory alignment ensures optimal blit performance for different color depths\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1c (28) - X offset field in BinkBuffer structure\n0x20 (32) - Y offset field in BinkBuffer structure  \n0x80 (128) - Clipping enabled flag field in BinkBuffer structure\n0x04 (4) - Y position field in BinkBuffer structure\n0x0 (0) - X position field in BinkBuffer structure\nMode 4 - 16-bit video memory (2-byte alignment)\nMode 3 - 24-bit video memory (8-byte alignment)\nOther - 32-bit video memory (4-byte alignment)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | nPosX      | int  | Buffer X position on screen\n0x04   | 4    | nPosY      | int  | Buffer Y position on screen\n0x1C   | 4    | nOffsetX   | int  | X offset within buffer\n0x20   | 4    | nOffsetY   | int  | Y offset within buffer\n0x80   | 4    | bClipping  | int  | Clipping enabled flag (0=disabled, non-zero=enabled)",
