      "name": "ClearVideoBufferByFormat",
      "signature": "void ClearVideoBufferByFormat(BYTE * pBuffer, dword nPixelFormat, dword nStride, dword nWidth, dword nHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Clears video buffer memory with format-specific fill patterns.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract pixel format from lower 4 bits of nPixelFormat parameter\n2. Switch on format to determine clearing strategy and fill values\n3. For format 0-6: Calculate total bytes using g_dwVideoMemory multiplier\n4. For format 8: Fill with 16-bit pattern 0x8000 (signed 16-bit midpoint)\n5. For format 9: Fill with 16-bit pattern 0x0080 (8-bit midpoint in 16-bit)\n6. For format 10: Two-pass clear - first pass 0x10, second pass 0x80\n7. Use optimized DWORD fills followed by byte remainder fills\n8. Advance buffer pointer by stride for each row\n\nParameters:\npBuffer: Target video buffer to clear (BYTE *)\nnPixelFormat: Pixel format flags, lower 4 bits determine clear pattern (dword)\nnStride: Bytes per row including padding (dword)\nnWidth: Width in pixels (dword)\nnHeight: Number of rows to clear (dword)\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFormat 0: Zero fill, uses g_dwVideoMemory * width for total bytes\nFormats 1-6: Same as format 0 (zero fill with video memory scaling)\nFormat 8: 16-bit signed midpoint fill (0x8000)\nFormat 9: 8-bit midpoint in 16-bit words (0x0080)\nFormat 10: Two-pass clearing with different patterns per pass\nOther formats: No operation (early return)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xF: Mask to extract lower 4 bits for format selection\n0x80008000: Packed dual 16-bit signed midpoint values\n0x800080: Packed 16-bit values with 8-bit midpoint\n0x10101010: Packed bytes with value 0x10 for first pass\n0x80808080: Packed bytes with value 0x80 for second pass\n\nError Handling:\nIf nHeight is 0, function returns immediately\nInvalid formats (7, 11-15) result in no operation\nBuffer pointer is not validated for NULL",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:faf5bb396f76b407fd98719b3b34ce15",
