      "name": "BinkBufferClose",
      "signature": "void BinkBufferClose(BinkBufferStruct * pBinkBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Releases and cleans up all resources associated with a Bink video buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate buffer pointer and ensure it contains valid data\n2. Release DirectX/DirectDraw surface interfaces if allocated\n3. Clean up graphics device contexts, bitmaps, and GDI objects\n4. Release DirectDraw resources if flag is set (offset 0x84)\n5. Restore display settings if flag is set (offset 0x88)  \n6. Zero out entire buffer structure (0x29 dwords = 164 bytes)\n7. Free the buffer memory block\n\nParameters:\npBinkBuffer - Pointer to BinkBufferStruct containing video playback resources and state flags\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function performs cleanup operations only\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pBinkBuffer is NULL or buffer data is invalid, function returns immediately without cleanup\n- DirectX surface release uses method calls through vtable offsets 0x84 and 0x8\n- Graphics cleanup only occurs if device context handle is non-zero\n- Flag at offset 0x84 indicates DirectDraw resources need cleanup\n- Flag at offset 0x88 indicates display settings restoration required\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name        | Type  | Description\n-------|------|------------------|-------|---------------------------\n0x48   | 4    | pDirectXInterface| void* | DirectX surface interface\n0x64   | 4    | dwSurfaceFlags   | uint  | DirectX surface status flags\n0x84   | 4    | dwDirectDrawFlag | uint  | DirectDraw cleanup required\n0x88   | 4    | dwDisplayFlag    | uint  | Display settings cleanup flag  \n0x8C   | 4    | hBitmap          | uint  | GDI bitmap object handle\n0x98   | 4    | pMemoryBuffer    | void* | Memory buffer for bitmap data\n0x9C   | 4    | dwDeviceContext  | uint  | Graphics device context handle\n0xA0   | 4    | hOrigBitmap      | uint  | Original bitmap selection\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x84 - DirectX interface vtable offset for Release method\n0x8 - DirectX interface vtable offset for cleanup method  \n0x200 - DirectX surface release parameter flag\n0x29 - Structure size in dwords (41 * 4 = 164 bytes)",
