      "name": "BinkBufferBlit",
      "signature": "void BinkBufferBlit(uint * pBinkBuffer, int * pnRectArray, uint dwRectCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Blits Bink video frame data to display surface using appropriate rendering method.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters (buffer pointer and rectangle count)\n2. Check buffer rendering mode and branch accordingly:\n   - Mode 1 (offset 0x64): Direct3D texture rendering with SetTexture/DrawPrimitive calls\n   - Mode 2 (offset 0x68): Direct3D surface rendering with scaled coordinate calculations  \n   - Mode 3 (offset 0x8C): GDI StretchBlt rendering for software fallback\n3. For each rendering mode, iterate through rectangle array if provided\n4. Calculate source and destination coordinates with scaling transformations\n5. Execute appropriate rendering call based on detected mode\n6. Clean up resources (release device contexts, restore texture state)\n\nParameters:\npBinkBuffer (uint *): Pointer to Bink video buffer structure containing:\n  - Rendering mode flags at various offsets (0x64, 0x68, 0x8C)\n  - Source dimensions and coordinates (offsets 0x3C, 0x40, 0x50, 0x54)\n  - Device handles and surface pointers\npnRectArray (int *): Pointer to array of rectangle structures (16 bytes each) or NULL for full frame\ndwRectCount (uint): Number of rectangles in array, or 0 to blit entire frame\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value, performs rendering operation directly\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pBinkBuffer is NULL or dwRectCount is 0, function returns without action\n- When pnRectArray is NULL, blits entire frame using buffer dimensions\n- Each rectangle array entry contains: srcX, srcY, width, height (4 DWORDs)\n- Coordinate scaling uses 64-bit arithmetic to prevent overflow\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x64 (100): Texture rendering mode flag offset\n0x68 (104): Surface rendering mode flag offset  \n0x8C (140): GDI rendering mode flag offset\n0x1000400: Direct3D primitive flags for texture mode\n0x1000000: Direct3D primitive flags for surface mode\n0xCC0020: GDI StretchBlt mode (SRCCOPY with color key)\n0x3: SetStretchBltMode parameter (COLORONCOLOR)\n0x10 (16): Size of each rectangle structure in bytes\n\nError Handling:\n- NULL pointer validation at function entry\n- Zero rectangle count causes immediate return\n- Missing rendering modes fall through to function exit\n- Device context allocation failures handled by Windows GDI\n\nStructure Layout:\nBinkBuffer offsets (accessed as DWORD array):\nOffset | Field | Type | Description\n0x00   | srcWidth | uint | Source buffer width in pixels\n0x04   | srcHeight | uint | Source buffer height in pixels  \n0x3C   | frameWidth | uint | Current frame width\n0x40   | frameHeight | uint | Current frame height\n0x4C   | textureHandle | uint | Direct3D texture handle\n0x50   | frameX | uint | Frame X position\n0x54   | frameY | uint | Frame Y position\n0x58   | destX | uint | Destination X coordinate\n0x5C   | destY | uint | Destination Y coordinate\n0x60   | windowHandle | uint | Window handle for GDI mode\n0x64   | textureMode | uint | Texture rendering enabled flag\n0x68   | surfaceMode | uint | Surface rendering enabled flag\n0x8C   | gdiMode | uint | GDI rendering enabled flag\n0x9C   | surfaceDC | uint | Surface device context handle",
