      "name": "BinkDDSurfaceType",
      "signature": "uint BinkDDSurfaceType(IDirectDrawSurface * pSurface)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Determines DirectDraw surface pixel format type by analyzing format structure\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate surface pointer is not NULL\n2. Initialize local DDPIXELFORMAT structure with size field set to 0x20\n3. Call surface's GetPixelFormat method via COM interface at vtable+0x54\n4. Check FourCC codes for YUV formats:\n   - 0x59565955 (UYVY) \u2192 return 9\n   - 0x32315659 (YV12) \u2192 return 10  \n   - 0x32595559 (UYVY) \u2192 return 8\n5. Check RGB bit depths:\n   - 8-bit \u2192 return 7\n   - 24-bit \u2192 return 1\n   - 32-bit \u2192 return 2\n6. Check RGB bit masks for 16-bit formats:\n   - R=0xF800, G=0x7E0, B=0x1F \u2192 16-bit 565 format \u2192 return 4\n   - R=0x7C00, G=0x3E0, B=0x1F \u2192 15-bit 555 format \u2192 return 3\n   - R=0xFC00, G=0x3E0, B=0x1F \u2192 16-bit 655 format \u2192 return 5\n   - R=0xFC00, G=0x3F0, B=0xF \u2192 12-bit 444 format \u2192 return 6\n7. Return 0xFFFFFFFF for unrecognized or invalid formats\n\nParameters:\npSurface (IDirectDrawSurface*): DirectDraw surface interface pointer\n\nReturns:\nuint: Surface format type code:\n  1 = 24-bit RGB\n  2 = 32-bit RGB\n  3 = 15-bit RGB (555)\n  4 = 16-bit RGB (565) \n  5 = 16-bit RGB (655)\n  6 = 12-bit RGB (444)\n  7 = 8-bit indexed\n  8 = UYVY YUV format\n  9 = UYVY YUV format (alternate)\n  10 = YV12 YUV format\n  0xFFFFFFFF = Invalid/unrecognized format\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL surface pointer returns 0xFFFFFFFF\n- Unrecognized FourCC codes fall through to RGB analysis\n- Bit mask validation requires exact matches for R, G, B components\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x20 (32): Size of DDPIXELFORMAT structure in bytes\n0x54 (84): Offset to GetPixelFormat method in DirectDraw surface vtable\n0x59565955: FourCC 'UYVY' (packed YUV 4:2:2)\n0x32315659: FourCC 'YV12' (planar YUV 4:2:0)  \n0x32595559: FourCC 'UYVY' (packed YUV 4:2:2 alternate)\n0xF800: 16-bit red mask for 565 format (bits 15-11)\n0x7E0: 16-bit green mask for 565 format (bits 10-5)\n0x1F: 16-bit blue mask for 565/555 formats (bits 4-0)\n0x7C00: 15-bit red mask for 555 format (bits 14-10)\n0x3E0: 15-bit green mask for 555 format (bits 9-5)\n0xFC00: Red mask for 655/444 formats\n0x3F0: Green mask for 444 format\n0xF: Blue mask for 444 format\n\nStructure Layout:\nDDPIXELFORMAT (32 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name      Type    Description\n0x00    4     dwSize          uint    Structure size (always 0x20)\n0x04    4     dwFlags         uint    Format flags (DDPF_*)\n0x08    4     dwFourCC        uint    FourCC code for compressed formats\n0x0C    4     dwRGBBitCount   uint    Bits per pixel for RGB formats\n0x10    4     dwRBitMask      uint    Red component bit mask\n0x14    4     dwGBitMask      uint    Green component bit mask  \n0x18    4     dwBBitMask      uint    Blue component bit mask\n0x1C    4     dwAlphaBitMask  uint    Alpha component bit mask",
