      "name": "TrackMemoryAllocation",
      "signature": "void TrackMemoryAllocation(uint dwAllocHandle, int nSizeBytes)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Records memory allocation information in global tracking arrays for Bink video codec memory management.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate 16-byte aligned block size from requested allocation size (add 15 and mask with 0xFFFFFFF0)\n2. Perform buddy allocator block positioning calculation using bit operations to find optimal placement\n3. Extract bucket index from current position using right shift by 5 bits (divide by 32)\n4. Extract offset within bucket from aligned size using right shift by 5 and mask with 0x1F\n5. Calculate distance between current bucket and target bucket, add 1, mask to 5 bits\n6. Multiply bucket distance by 32 bytes (left shift by 5) to get byte offset adjustment\n7. Add byte offset adjustment to aligned block size to get final allocation size\n8. Update global current allocation position by adding calculated allocation size\n9. Store allocation size in global size array at current entry index\n10. Store allocation handle in global handle array at current entry index\n11. Increment global allocation entry count for next allocation\n\nParameters:\ndwAllocHandle - Handle or identifier value associated with this memory allocation (stored in tracking array)\nnSizeBytes - Requested allocation size in bytes (will be aligned to 16-byte boundary)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function tracks allocation but returns no status\n\nSpecial Cases:\nBuddy allocator bit manipulation ensures optimal block placement for memory fragmentation reduction\n16-byte alignment (0xFFFFFFF0 mask) required for SIMD operations and performance optimization\nBucket size is fixed at 32 bytes (0x20) for consistent block management\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xF (15) - Alignment padding to round up to next 16-byte boundary\n0xFFFFFFF0 - 16-byte alignment mask (clears bottom 4 bits)\n0x5 (5) - Right shift count to divide by 32 (bucket size calculation)\n0x1F (31) - 5-bit mask for modulo 32 operations (bucket offset extraction)\n0x20 (32) - Bucket size in bytes for memory block management",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:2e320bf81519acea38e6c31a9369e455",
