      "name": "BinkSetError",
      "signature": "void BinkSetError(char * lpszErrorMessage)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets the global error message buffer for Bink video library.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate length of input error message string using SCASB.REPNE instruction\n2. Restore source pointer to beginning of string after length calculation\n3. Copy error message to global buffer using optimized 32-bit dword copy (MOVSD.REP)  \n4. Copy remaining bytes using byte-wise copy (MOVSB.REP) for unaligned remainder\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  lpszErrorMessage (char *): Pointer to null-terminated error message string to copy\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function assumes lpszErrorMessage points to valid null-terminated string\n- No bounds checking performed - caller must ensure string fits in 256-byte buffer\n- Function will overwrite any existing error message in global buffer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x1002f568: Address of global error message buffer (g_abErrorBuffer)\n  0xffffffff: Initial value for length calculation (-1)  \n  0x2: Right shift count for dword copy optimization (divide by 4)\n  0x3: Mask for remaining bytes after dword copy (modulo 4)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "EXP",
