      "name": "BinkPositionFrame",
      "signature": "void BinkPositionFrame(BinkFileHandle * pBinkHandle, int nFrameIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Positions a Bink video file to a specific frame for playback operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate and adjust frame index (decrement if non-zero for 0-based indexing)\n2. Process current frame if frame handler is active (reserved2[1] != -1)\n3. Update internal position tracking (pfnClose = pfnTell)\n4. Handle special case for frame 0 (beginning):\n   - Reset sound state if sound is enabled (reserved1[1] != 0)\n   - Clear status flags (dwFileSize = 0)\n5. Calculate frame positioning based on indexing mode:\n   - Direct mode (pfnRead == NULL): Use frame offset table and callback\n   - Buffered mode: Calculate relative offset from base position\n6. Process frame again to ensure consistent state\n7. Update current frame counter (pfnTell = nFrameIndex + 1)\n\nParameters:\npBinkHandle (BinkFileHandle*): Pointer to Bink video file handle containing frame data, position tracking, and callback functions\nnFrameIndex (int): Target frame number to position to (0-based indexing)\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFrame 0 handling: Resets sound state and clears status flags for playback restart\nFrame offset masking: Uses 0xFFFFFFFE mask to align frame offsets to even boundaries\nDual processing: Calls ProcessBinkFrame before and after positioning for state consistency\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xFFFFFFFF: Invalid frame handler indicator (reserved2[1] check)\n0xFFFFFFFE: Frame offset alignment mask (ensures even byte boundaries)\n0x0: Sound off parameter for _BinkSetSoundOnOff\n0x1: Sound on parameter for _BinkSetSoundOnOff\n\nError Handling:\nFunction assumes valid BinkFileHandle pointer and frame index within file bounds\nNo explicit error checking - relies on caller validation\nFrame handler state managed through reserved2[1] field checking\n\nStructure Layout:\nBinkFileHandle offsets (key fields):\nOffset 0x00: pfnTell (current position function pointer)\nOffset 0x10: pfnClose (close function pointer) \nOffset 0x104: dwFileSize (file size/status)\nOffset 0x108: pfnRead (read mode indicator)\nOffset 0x10C: pfnWrite (frame table pointer)\nOffset 0x114: pfnSeek (positioning callback)\nOffset 0x1E8: reserved2[1] (frame handler state)\nOffset 0x22C: reserved1[1] (sound enable state)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
