      "name": "ProcessBinkFrame",
      "signature": "void ProcessBinkFrame(BinkDecoder * pBinkDecoder)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes a single frame of Bink video data with thread-safe buffer management.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment lock counter to prevent concurrent access to decoder state\n2. Check if this is the first thread accessing the decoder (lock counter == 1)\n3. Call frame initialization callback if available to prepare frame processing\n4. Validate buffer state and frame timing conditions before proceeding\n5. Execute read callback to fetch frame data into internal buffers\n6. Check if frame advance is required based on timing thresholds\n7. Update frame timing statistics and reset processing flags if needed\n8. Call decoder read callback to get processed frame data\n9. Handle double-buffering if enabled (multiply byte counts by 2)\n10. Determine actual bytes to copy based on buffer availability\n11. Copy data from internal buffers to destination using optimized routines\n12. Update buffer pointers and remaining capacity after copy operation\n13. Call advance callback to signal completion of frame processing\n14. Loop back to step 5 until no more data available for current frame\n15. Decrement lock counter to release access to decoder state\n\nParameters:\npBinkDecoder - Pointer to BinkDecoder structure containing:\n  - Lock counter at offset 0x29C for thread synchronization\n  - Function pointers for frame, read, and advance callbacks\n  - Buffer management pointers (start, current, end positions)\n  - Double buffering flag and timing state information\n  - Frame counters and timing thresholds for rate control\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return error codes, uses internal state flags\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Exits early if lock counter indicates another thread is processing\n- Skips processing if buffer size insufficient or frame limits exceeded  \n- Handles partial buffer copies when available data < requested amount\n- Uses memory copy optimization (MOVSD.REP) for 4-byte aligned transfers\n- Falls back to byte-level copying (MOVSB.REP) for remaining bytes\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x29C (668) - Offset to lock counter byte in BinkDecoder structure\n0x2A4 (676) - Offset to frame callback function pointer\n0x2A8 (680) - Offset to read callback function pointer  \n0x2AC (684) - Offset to advance callback function pointer\n0x298 (664) - Offset to available buffer size in bytes\n0x2A0 (672) - Offset to double buffering enabled flag\n0x290 (656) - Offset to current buffer position pointer\n0x288 (648) - Offset to buffer end boundary pointer\n0x284 (644) - Offset to buffer start pointer\n0x2EE (750) - Frame timing increment in milliseconds",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
