      "name": "ClearBinkDecoderBuffers",
      "signature": "void ClearBinkDecoderBuffers(BinkDecoder * pDecoder)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Clears memory buffers in a Bink decoder's circular buffer system when decoder position is behind the target position.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if decoder current position (offset 0x298) is less than target position (offset 0x370)\n2. If not behind target, exit early (no clearing needed)\n3. Calculate bytes to clear as difference between target and current positions\n4. Get buffer end pointer (offset 0x284) and calculate new current pointer position\n5. Update current pointer (offset 0x290) by subtracting bytes to clear\n6. Check if new pointer position wraps below buffer start\n7. If wraparound occurs:\n   a. Calculate wraparound bytes (distance from new pointer to buffer end)\n   b. Calculate remaining bytes to clear after wraparound\n   c. Set current pointer to wrapped position (buffer start + pointer offset)\n   d. Clear wraparound region at buffer end using DWORD and byte clearing loops\n   e. Update pointer to buffer start for remaining clearing\n8. Clear main region using optimized DWORD clearing (4-byte chunks)\n9. Clear remaining bytes (0-3 bytes) using byte-by-byte clearing\n10. Update decoder current position by adding bytes cleared\n\nParameters:\npDecoder - Pointer to BinkDecoder structure containing circular buffer state\n  Offset 0x280: Buffer start address\n  Offset 0x284: Buffer end pointer  \n  Offset 0x290: Current buffer pointer\n  Offset 0x298: Current decoder position (bytes)\n  Offset 0x370: Target decoder position (bytes)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, modifies decoder buffer state in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If current position >= target position, function exits immediately\n- Handles circular buffer wraparound by clearing in two regions\n- Optimizes clearing using DWORD operations followed by byte cleanup\n- Buffer pointers are managed as byte pointers for precise positioning\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x280 (640) - Offset to buffer start address in BinkDecoder\n0x284 (644) - Offset to buffer end pointer in BinkDecoder  \n0x290 (656) - Offset to current buffer pointer in BinkDecoder\n0x298 (664) - Offset to current position counter in BinkDecoder\n0x370 (880) - Offset to target position counter in BinkDecoder\n0x2 (2) - Right shift count for DWORD clearing (divide by 4)\n0x3 (3) - Mask for remaining bytes after DWORD clearing\n\nStructure Layout:\nBinkDecoder (partial - relevant fields):\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type      Description\n+0x280  4     pBufferStart        byte*     Start of circular buffer\n+0x284  4     pBufferEnd          byte*     End of circular buffer  \n+0x290  4     pCurrentPtr         byte*     Current position in buffer\n+0x298  4     dwCurrentPosition   uint      Current decoder position (bytes)\n+0x370  4     dwTargetPosition    uint      Target decoder position (bytes)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
