      "name": "ProcessBinkVideoFrames",
      "signature": "void ProcessBinkVideoFrames(int * pBinkDecoder)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Main video frame processing loop for Bink decoder with timing control.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate decoder state - exit if not in active playback state (state != 1)\n2. Enter main processing loop\n3. Check if frame processing conditions are met:\n   - Bit 0x8000000 not set in flags at offset 0x20\n   - Error state at offset 0x108 is clear (== 0)\n4. If conditions met, call frame callback function at offset 0x120\n5. Calculate frame rate percentage: (frames_displayed + 1) * 100 / (total_frames + 1)\n6. If frame rate > 50% (0x32), sleep for 5ms, otherwise sleep for 10ms\n7. Get current system time with timeGetTime()\n8. If 10ms elapsed since last frame and decoder active (offset 0x1E8 != -1):\n   - Call ProcessBinkFrame to decode and display next frame\n9. Re-check decoder state, exit if changed from active (state != 1)\n10. Repeat loop indefinitely until state change\n\nParameters:\npBinkDecoder - Pointer to BinkDecoder structure containing:\n  - Offset 0x20: Control flags (bit 0x8000000 = processing disabled)\n  - Offset 0x108: Error status (0 = no error)\n  - Offset 0x120: Frame callback function pointer\n  - Offset 0x150: Total frames count\n  - Offset 0x154: Frames displayed count\n  - Offset 0x1E8: Active frame index (-1 = inactive)\n  - Offset 0x250: Decoder state (1 = active, 2 = stopped)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function runs until decoder state changes from active to stopped\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Frame rate calculation prevents overflow by adding 1 to both numerator and denominator\n- Sleep duration of 5ms vs 10ms provides adaptive frame rate control\n- State 2 indicates stopped/cleanup state vs state 1 for active playback\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x8000000 (134217728) - Processing disable flag bit\n0x32 (50) - Frame rate threshold percentage for sleep timing\n0x5 (5) - Fast sleep duration in milliseconds for high frame rates\n0xa (10) - Standard sleep duration in milliseconds\n0x1 (1) - Active decoder state\n0x2 (2) - Stopped decoder state\n-1 (0xFFFFFFFF) - Inactive frame index marker",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:18a88b63ec9207e96cdbf1f45be2b683",
