      "name": "BinkCopyToBuffer",
      "signature": "int BinkCopyToBuffer(BinkDecoder * pBinkDecoder, uint dwDestBuffer, int nPitch, int nHeight, uint dwDestX, uint dwDestY, uint dwFormatFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Copies decoded Bink video frame to destination buffer with format conversion and timing control.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters - return 0 if pBinkDecoder or dwDestBuffer is null\n2. Set decoder busy flag at offset 0x4d to prevent concurrent access\n3. Extract blit format from lower 4 bits of dwFormatFlags\n4. Combine format flags with decoder flags at offset 0x8 (bits 0x70030000)\n5. Initialize YUV conversion system with the extracted format\n6. Handle negative pitch - adjust buffer pointer for bottom-up DIB format\n7. Process frame timing and synchronization if frame index != -1\n8. Calculate target display time based on frame rate and current frame\n9. Check if frame should be dropped for performance (< 10% CPU usage)\n10. Implement frame rate control with Sleep() calls and buffer clearing\n11. Determine blit path - masked vs direct based on string buffer and format flags\n12. Execute appropriate YUV blit function based on pixel format\n13. Continue frame processing if frame index indicates more frames available\n14. Clear decoder busy flag and return success status\n\nParameters:\npBinkDecoder - Pointer to BinkDecoder structure containing video state\ndwDestBuffer - Destination buffer memory address for video output\nnPitch - Bytes per scanline (negative for bottom-up DIBs)\nnHeight - Height in pixels of destination rectangle\ndwDestX - X coordinate in destination buffer\ndwDestY - Y coordinate in destination buffer  \ndwFormatFlags - Combined format and control flags\n\nReturns:\n1 - Success, frame copied to destination buffer\n0 - Failure, null pointers or invalid parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNegative nPitch: Bottom-up DIB format, adjusts buffer pointer by ((nHeight - dwDestY) - 1) * |nPitch|\nFrame Dropping: CPU usage < 10% triggers frame skip with pause/resume cycle\nTiming Control: Decoder waits if frame display time hasn't arrived\nString Buffer: Empty string at offset 0x37 triggers direct blit instead of masked\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x4d (308) - Decoder busy flag offset\n0x8 (32) - Decoder flags offset, bits 0x70030000 mask\n0x70030000 - Decoder capability flags mask\n0xf (15) - Blit format mask for lower 4 bits\n0x80000 (524288) - Skip timing check flag\n0x80000000 (2147483648) - Direct blit vs masked blit flag\n0x37 (220) - String buffer pointer offset\n0x7a (488) - Frame index offset (-1 indicates no more frames)\n0x83 (524) - Last frame time offset\n0x84 (528) - Frame duration offset\n0x85 (532) - Frame skip threshold offset\n\nBlit Format Mapping:\n1 - 24bpp RGB format\n2 - 32bpp RGBA format  \n3-6 - 16bpp RGB formats (565, 555, etc.)\n8 - YUY2 packed format\n9 - UYVY packed format\n10 - YV12 planar format",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
