      "name": "BinkDoFrame",
      "signature": "int BinkDoFrame(BinkDecoder * pBinkDecoder)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Processes the next frame in a Bink video stream and manages timing, buffering, and decompression.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate decoder pointer and check if current frame equals total frames (stream complete)\n2. Set processing flag and capture current timestamp using timeGetTime()\n3. Initialize circular buffer headers for 7 data streams (0x97-0x9d offsets)  \n4. Copy timing values into buffer headers for frame synchronization\n5. If first frame processing, calculate frame timing offset using 1000ms denominator\n6. Process active frame data if streaming index is valid (not -1)\n7. Iterate through frame data packets and handle buffer decompression\n8. Use atomic lock operations to synchronize memory buffer access\n9. Copy decompressed data between ring buffers with 4-byte and byte-level transfers\n10. Clear video buffer memory if required (16-pixel aligned dimensions)\n11. Apply frame rate throttling via Sleep(0) when processing load < 75%\n12. Call ExpandBinkPlanes() for YUV plane decompression and color conversion\n13. Update frame counters, timing metrics, and decoder state\n14. Return 0 for success\n\nParameters:\npBinkDecoder (BinkDecoder*): Main decoder context containing stream data, buffers, timing info, and processing state\n\nReturns:\n0 (int): Success status - function always returns 0\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3E8 (1000): Millisecond conversion factor for timing calculations\n0x8000000 (0x8000000): Decoder flags bit mask for processing mode check  \n0x4B (75): Frame rate threshold percentage for throttling decisions\n\nError Handling:\n- Returns 0 immediately if decoder pointer is null\n- Returns 0 if current frame equals total frames (end of stream)\n- Atomic lock operations prevent race conditions during buffer access\n- Buffer boundary checks prevent memory overwrites during data copying",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
