      "name": "BinkGetKeyFrame",
      "signature": "uint BinkGetKeyFrame(BinkHandle * pBinkHandle, uint dwStartFrame, uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Searches for the nearest keyframe in a Bink video stream.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters (null check on Bink handle)\n2. Check if force flag (0x80) is set or current frame is not a keyframe\n3. Extract search direction from flags (bits 0-6)\n4. If search direction = 1: Search forward from start frame for next keyframe\n5. If search direction = 2: Search bidirectionally (backward then forward)\n6. If search direction = 0: Search backward from start frame for previous keyframe\n7. For each frame, check keyframe flag (bit 0) in frame array at offset 0x10c\n8. Return frame number when keyframe found, or 0 if none found\n\nParameters:\npBinkHandle (BinkHandle *) - Pointer to Bink video handle structure\ndwStartFrame (uint) - Starting frame number for search (1-based)\ndwFlags (uint) - Search control flags:\n  - Bit 7 (0x80): Force flag - always search regardless of current frame\n  - Bits 0-6: Search direction (0=backward, 1=forward, 2=bidirectional)\n\nReturns:\nFrame number (1-based) of nearest keyframe\n0 if no keyframe found or invalid parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\nReturns current frame if already a keyframe and force flag not set\nBidirectional search checks backward first, then forward if not found\nForward search stops at total frame count (dwTotalFrames field)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x80 (128) - Force search flag mask  \n0x7F (127) - Search direction mask\n0x10c (268) - Offset to frame array pointer in Bink handle\n0x8 (8) - Offset to total frame count in Bink handle\n0x1 (1) - Keyframe flag bit in frame data\n\nStructure Layout:\nBinkHandle Structure:\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type  | Description\n+0x8   | 4    | dwTotalFrames   | uint  | Total number of frames\n+0x10c | 4    | pFrameArray     | uint* | Pointer to frame data array\n\nFrame Array Entry:\nBit 0: Keyframe flag (1=keyframe, 0=normal frame)\nBits 1-31: Additional frame metadata",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "EXP",
      "index": "EXP:22",
