      "name": "BinkClose",
      "signature": "void BinkClose(byte * pBinkDecoder)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Closes and cleans up a Bink video decoder, releasing all associated resources\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input pointer is not NULL, return early if invalid\n2. Pause the decoder using BinkPause to stop any active playback\n3. Wait for thread synchronization if decoder was actively playing (offset 0x250 == 1)\n4. Close thread handle at offset 0x100 if present using FUN_1000ab00\n5. Close file handle and callbacks if file handle at offset 0x1e8 != -1\n6. Determine which memory buffer to free based on ownership flags\n7. Free primary memory buffer from offset 0x108 or alternate from offset 0x1d8\n8. Free secondary memory buffer at offset 0x284 if allocated\n9. Zero entire decoder structure (0xe7 dwords = 924 bytes)\n10. Free the decoder structure itself using RadFree\n\nParameters:\npBinkDecoder - Pointer to BinkDecoder structure containing decoder state, passed as byte pointer for structure access\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pointer check prevents crashes on invalid input\n- Thread synchronization prevents resource conflicts during shutdown\n- Memory ownership flag at offset 0x20 bit 0x4000000 controls freeing behavior\n- File handle value -1 indicates no file is open\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x250 (592) - Thread active flag (1 = active, 0 = inactive)\n0x100 (256) - Thread handle storage offset\n0x1e8 (488) - File handle storage offset  \n0x108 (264) - Primary memory buffer pointer offset\n0x1d8 (472) - Alternate memory buffer pointer offset\n0x284 (644) - Secondary memory buffer pointer offset\n0x20 (32) - Decoder flags offset\n0x4000000 - Memory ownership flag bit\n0xe7 (231) - Structure size in dwords for zeroing\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x20   | 4    | dwFlags    | byte | Decoder control flags including memory ownership\n0x100  | 4    | hThread    | byte | Thread handle for async operations\n0x108  | 4    | pMemory1   | byte | Primary memory buffer pointer\n0x1d8  | 4    | pMemory2   | byte | Alternate memory buffer pointer  \n0x1e8  | 4    | hFile      | byte | File handle (-1 if no file)\n0x250  | 4    | bActive    | byte | Thread activity flag (1=active, 0=inactive)\n0x284  | 4    | pMemory3   | byte | Secondary memory buffer pointer\n0x294  | 4    | hCallback  | byte | Callback handle for file operations\n0x2a4  | 4    | callbackData | byte | Callback data structure\n0x2c0  | 4    | pfnClose   | byte | Function pointer for close callback",
