      "comment": "Extracts comprehensive summary statistics from a Bink video decoder instance\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate decoder and summary pointers are non-null\n2. Get current system time for timing calculations \n3. Update decoder timing statistics and frame timing\n4. Initialize summary structure by clearing 31 DWORDs (124 bytes)\n5. Copy video dimensions from decoder offsets 0x14, 0x18\n6. Copy frame rate information from decoder offsets 0x364, 0x368, 0x248, 0x24c\n7. Copy current frame from decoder offset 0x8\n8. Calculate elapsed playback time (current time - start time at 0x200)\n9. Copy playback statistics from decoder offsets 0x244, 0x23c-0x240\n10. Accumulate skipped frame count from decoder offset 0x234\n11. Calculate frame rate as (frame_numerator * 1000) / (frame_denominator + 1)\n12. Copy decompression statistics from decoder offsets 0x4f-0x51  \n13. Calculate buffer usage: (total_buffer - (current_pos & 0xfffffffe))\n14. Calculate compression ratio: (buffer_bytes * frame_width) / (frame_height * current_frame)\n15. Calculate frames per second: buffer_bytes / current_frame\n16. Copy additional statistics from decoder offsets 0x3d, 0x3e\n17. Copy base video dimensions and playback state\n18. Copy decoder performance statistics from offsets 0x87-0x8a, 0x52-0x53\n\nParameters:\npDecoder - Pointer to BinkDecoder structure containing video state and statistics\npSummary - Pointer to BinkSummary structure to receive extracted statistics\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If either pDecoder or pSummary is NULL, function returns immediately without processing\n- Frame rate calculation adds 1 to denominator to prevent division by zero\n- Buffer position is masked with 0xfffffffe to align to even addresses\n- Accumulated skipped frame count is added to existing value in summary\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1f (31) - Number of DWORDs to clear in summary structure\n0x364 - Decoder offset for frame width statistics  \n0x368 - Decoder offset for frame height statistics\n0x248 - Decoder offset for frame rate numerator\n0x24c - Decoder offset for frame rate denominator\n0x200 - Decoder offset for playback start time\n0x234 - Decoder offset for skipped frame accumulator\n1000 - Milliseconds multiplier for frame rate calculation\n0xfffffffe - Mask for even-byte buffer alignment\n\nStructure Layout:\nBinkSummary (124 bytes total):\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type    Description\n0x00    4     dwWidth                 uint    Video width in pixels  \n0x04    4     dwHeight                uint    Video height in pixels\n0x08    4     dwElapsedTime           uint    Elapsed playback time in milliseconds\n0x0c    4     dwFrameWidth            uint    Frame buffer width\n0x10    4     dwFrameHeight           uint    Frame buffer height  \n0x14    4     dwOriginalWidth         uint    Original video width\n0x18    4     dwOriginalHeight        uint    Original video height\n0x1c    4     dwPlaybackRate          uint    Current playback rate\n0x20    4     dwCurrentFrame          uint    Current frame number\n0x24    4     dwTotalFrames           uint    Total frame count\n0x28    4     dwFrameRateNumerator    uint    Frame rate numerator\n0x2c    4     dwFrameRateDenominator  uint    Frame rate denominator  \n0x30    4     dwSkippedFrames         uint    Number of skipped frames\n0x34    4     dwDecompressedFrames    uint    Number of decompressed frames\n0x38    4     dwBufferSize            uint    Decoder buffer size\n0x3c    4     dwBufferUsed            uint    Bytes used in buffer\n0x40    4     dwFramesDecompressed    uint    Total frames decompressed  \n0x44    4     dwFramesSkipped         uint    Total frames skipped\n0x48    4     dwBytesPerSecond        uint    Data throughput rate\n0x4c    4     dwFramesPerSecond       uint    Calculated frame rate\n0x50-0x74     dwField14-dwField1D     uint    Additional decoder statistics",
