      "name": "BinkGetRealtimeStatistics",
      "signature": "void BinkGetRealtimeStatistics(BinkDecoder * pBinkDecoder, uint * pdwOutputStats, uint dwFrameIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Retrieves real-time playback statistics and timing information from Bink video decoder.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Get current system time using timeGetTime()\n2. Update playback timing adjustments for the decoder\n3. Update frame timing statistics for performance monitoring\n4. Validate and clamp frame index to valid range\n5. Extract decoder state values into output statistics array\n6. Calculate differential statistics from frame timing arrays\n7. Store all computed statistics in caller-provided output array\n\nParameters:\n\npBinkDecoder: Pointer to BinkDecoder structure containing video stream state\npdwOutputStats: Pointer to uint array for storing 14 statistics values  \ndwFrameIndex: Zero-based frame index for historical comparison (0 = current frame)\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - Statistics are returned through pdwOutputStats array\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nFrame index validation prevents out-of-bounds array access\nTiming delta minimum value of 1 prevents division by zero in caller\nHistorical frame comparison uses validated index for safe array access\nComplex timing calculation uses 64-bit arithmetic to prevent overflow\n\nMagic Numbers:\n\n0x254 = Total frame count in decoder\n0x24c = Frame timing divisor for duration calculation  \n0x248 = Frame timing multiplier for duration calculation\n0x10c = Pointer to timing array for average calculation",
