      "name": "BinkGetRects",
      "signature": "uint BinkGetRects(uint * pBinkStruct, uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Calculate dirty rectangles for Bink video frame updates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters - return 0 if invalid flags (0x4000000) set\n2. Check if rectangle calculation should be skipped based on flags and state\n3. Return 0 if no scaling flags and texture cache disabled\n4. Initialize rectangle processing if rectangle count is unset (0xffffffff)\n5. Call FUN_1000a2d0 to calculate initial rectangle dimensions\n6. If expansion mode enabled, process rectangles iteratively using FUN_1000a430\n7. Find rectangle with highest priority in each iteration\n8. Split best rectangle and add new rectangles to processing queue\n9. Continue until 8 rectangles reached or no more splits possible\n10. Sort final rectangles by screen position (top-left first)\n11. Apply scaling transformation based on video format flags\n12. Clamp rectangle bounds to video frame dimensions\n13. Copy final rectangles to output buffer\n14. Return total number of rectangles processed\n\nParameters:\npBinkStruct (uint *): Pointer to Bink video decoder structure containing:\n  - [0x0]: Frame width for boundary clamping\n  - [0x1]: Frame height for boundary clamping  \n  - [0x8]: Scaling and format flags\n  - [0xd]: Base rectangle coordinates (x,y,w,h)\n  - [0x2d]: Current rectangle count (-1 = uninitialized)\n  - [0x33]: Initial rectangle width\n  - [0x34]: Initial rectangle height\n  - [0x37]: Processing width parameter\n  - [0x38]: Processing height parameter\n  - [0x9e]: Video format and scaling flags\n  - [0xd8]: Texture cache state\ndwFlags (uint): Processing control flags:\n  - 0x4000000: Skip processing (return 0)\n  - 0x80000: Force processing override\n  - 0x8000000: Disable rectangle expansion\n\nReturns:\nuint: Number of dirty rectangles calculated, or 0 if processing skipped\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 immediately if dwFlags has 0x4000000 bit set\n- Returns 0 if no scaling needed and texture cache disabled\n- Maximum of 8 rectangles can be processed in expansion mode\n- Rectangle coordinates scaled by 2x for certain video formats\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x4000000: Skip processing flag\n0x80000: Force processing flag  \n0x8000000: Disable expansion flag\n0xffffffff: Uninitialized rectangle count marker\n0x7fff0000: Large value for minimum position search\n0x70000000: Video format mask for scaling flags\n0x30000000: 2x width scaling format\n0x10000000, 0x20000000: XY scaling formats\n0x40000000, 0x50000000: 2x width+height scaling formats\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type    Description\n0x0     4     dwFrameWidth  uint    Frame width for clamping\n0x4     4     dwFrameHeight uint    Frame height for clamping  \n0x20    4     dwFlags       uint    Processing flags\n0x34    16    rectBase      uint[4] Base rectangle (x,y,w,h)\n0xb4    4     dwRectCount   uint    Current rectangle count\n0xcc    4     dwInitWidth   uint    Initial rectangle width\n0xd0    4     dwInitHeight  uint    Initial rectangle height\n0xdc    4     dwProcWidth   uint    Processing width\n0xe0    4     dwProcHeight  uint    Processing height\n0x278   4     dwVideoFormat uint    Video format and scaling flags\n0x360   4     dwCacheState  uint    Texture cache state",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
