      "name": "TrimBitmapBounds",
      "signature": "int TrimBitmapBounds(int * pDestRect, int nBitmapWidth, int nBitmapHeight, int * pSourceRect)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Analyzes bitmap buffer content and trims empty space from rectangle bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate starting buffer position from source rectangle coordinates (pixel coordinates converted to byte offsets with division by 16)\n2. Extract trimmed width and height dimensions from source rectangle, also divided by 16\n3. Scan row by row from top, checking each pixel column for non-null content\n4. If no content found in entire bitmap area, return 0 (empty bitmap)\n5. When first non-null content found, store row position and calculate buffer adjustments\n6. Update destination rectangle top coordinate (source top + found row * 16)\n7. Update destination rectangle bottom coordinate (source bottom - found row * 16)\n8. Validate remaining height is at least 2 pixels before continuing\n9. Scan from bottom upward to trim empty rows from bottom edge\n10. Update destination rectangle bottom coordinate after trimming bottom rows\n11. Scan column by column from left edge to find leftmost non-null content\n12. Update destination rectangle left coordinate (source left + found column * 16)\n13. Update destination rectangle right coordinate (source right - found column * 16)  \n14. Validate remaining width is at least 2 pixels before scanning right edge\n15. Scan from right edge leftward to trim empty columns from right side\n16. Update destination rectangle right coordinate after trimming right columns\n17. Return 1 to indicate successful trimming operation\n\nParameters:\npDestRect - Pointer to destination RECT structure to store trimmed bounds (left, top, right, bottom coordinates)\nnBitmapWidth - Width stride of bitmap buffer in bytes for row calculations\nnBitmapHeight - Height of bitmap area for boundary validation\npSourceRect - Pointer to source RECT structure with initial bounds (left, top, right, bottom coordinates)\n\nReturns:\n0 - Bitmap contains no non-null content (completely empty)\n1 - Successfully trimmed bounds and updated destination rectangle\n\nSpecial Cases:\nDivision by 16 (SAR 0x4) converts pixel coordinates to some internal coordinate system\nMultiplication by 16 (SHL 0x4) converts back when updating rectangle coordinates\nAlgorithm assumes bitmap buffer starts at calculated position based on source rectangle\nMinimum width/height of 2 required for edge trimming operations\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10 (16) - Coordinate scaling factor for pixel to internal unit conversion\n0x4 - Right shift amount for division by 16 (SAR 0x4 equivalent to / 16)\n0xF - Mask for rounding adjustment during signed division\n0x1F - Mask for 32-bit sign extension during division operations\n\nStructure Layout:\nRECT Structure (16 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | left       | int  | Left edge X coordinate\n0x04   | 4    | top        | int  | Top edge Y coordinate  \n0x08   | 4    | right      | int  | Right edge X coordinate\n0x0C   | 4    | bottom     | int  | Bottom edge Y coordinate",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b321489c43a17c8bc653c7614c1dc777",
