      "name": "BinkGetTrackMaxSize",
      "signature": "dword BinkGetTrackMaxSize(BinkObject * pBinkHandle, int nTrackIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Retrieves the maximum size for a specified audio track in a Bink video file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that pBinkHandle is not NULL\n2. If NULL, return 0 (error condition)\n3. Access track data structure at offset 0x1ec in Bink handle\n4. Calculate offset into track size array using nTrackIndex * 4\n5. Return the DWORD value at calculated offset\n\nParameters:\npBinkHandle (BinkObject*): Pointer to Bink video handle structure containing track metadata\nnTrackIndex (int): Zero-based index of audio track to query\n\nReturns:\nDWORD: Maximum size in bytes for the specified track, or 0 if invalid handle\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 if pBinkHandle is NULL (invalid handle)\n- No bounds checking on nTrackIndex (caller must ensure valid range)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1ec (492): Offset to track size array pointer within Bink handle structure\n0x4: Size of DWORD array elements (track size values)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
