      "name": "BinkOpenTrack",
      "signature": "BinkTrack * BinkOpenTrack(BINK * pBinkFile, uint dwTrackIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "BinkTrack *",
      "comment": "Opens and initializes a Bink video track for playback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters - ensure Bink file handle is non-null\n2. Verify track index is within valid range (< track count at offset 0xF0)\n3. Read track flags from track table and check if track is active (bit 31 set)\n4. Allocate resource handle using track ID and channel count via FUN_10019db0\n5. Allocate 28-byte track information structure using RadMalloc\n6. Initialize structure to zero using REP STOSD (7 DWORDs)\n7. Store Bink file handle and resource handle in structure\n8. Extract and store track configuration data (ID, bit depth, channels, stride)\n9. Apply special handling for 8-bit audio (halve stride value)\n10. Store track index and return pointer to initialized structure\n\nParameters:\npBinkFile (BINK*): Pointer to Bink file structure containing track metadata\ndwTrackIndex (uint): Zero-based track index to open\n\nReturns:\nSuccess: Pointer to allocated and initialized BinkTrack structure\nFailure: NULL if invalid parameters, track inactive, or allocation failed",
