      "name": "BinkGetTrackData",
      "signature": "char * BinkGetTrackData(int nBinkHandle, char * szOutputBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Extract and decode audio track data from Bink video file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate Bink handle is not null, return null if invalid\n2. Load track information structure from handle offset 0x10\n3. Get track data pointer array from track info offset 0x104\n4. Loop through available tracks (count at offset 0xf0)\n5. Compare current track index with requested track (handle offset 0x18)\n6. Skip tracks that don't match or have no data (first dword is 0)\n7. Initialize track data pointer to second dword of matching track\n8. Set processed data counter to 0 and output pointer to buffer start\n9. While bytes remain to process in current track segment:\n   a. Call FUN_10019ed0 to decompress next audio chunk\n   b. Clamp chunk size if it exceeds remaining bytes to process\n   c. Check audio format flag at handle offset 0x4\n   d. If format is 0x10 (16-bit): Copy decompressed data directly using DWORD/BYTE copy\n   e. If format is not 0x10 (8-bit): Convert 16-bit samples to 8-bit by shifting right 8 bits and adding 0x80\n   f. Update processed data counter and output buffer pointer\n   g. Continue until all bytes in track segment are processed\n10. Return total bytes processed for this track\n11. If no matching track found, return null\n\nParameters:\npBinkHandle (int): Pointer to Bink video file handle structure\npbOutputBuffer (char *): Destination buffer for decoded audio data\n\nReturns:\nchar *: Pointer indicating total bytes processed (pbProcessedData counter), or null if track not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns null immediately if pBinkHandle is null\n- Returns null if no tracks exist (track count <= 0)\n- Returns null if requested track index not found in track array\n- Returns null if matching track has no data (track data pointer is 0)\n- Handles both 16-bit (0x10) and 8-bit audio format conversion\n- 8-bit conversion: shifts 16-bit sample right 8 bits and adds 0x80 bias\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10: Offset to track information structure in Bink handle\n0x104: Offset to track data pointer array in track info\n0xf0: Offset to track count in track info structure\n0x18: Offset to requested track index in Bink handle\n0x4: Offset to audio format flag in Bink handle\n0x10: Audio format constant for 16-bit audio\n0x80: 8-bit audio bias value added during conversion\n\nStructure Layout:\nBink Handle Structure (pBinkHandle):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type | Description\n0x4    | 4    | dwAudioFormat | int  | Audio format (0x10 = 16-bit)\n0x10   | 4    | pTrackInfo    | ptr  | Pointer to track information\n0x18   | 4    | nTrackIndex   | int  | Requested track index\n\nTrack Info Structure:\nOffset | Size | Field Name     | Type | Description\n0xf0   | 4    | nTrackCount    | int  | Number of available tracks\n0x104  | 4    | pTrackDataArray| ptr  | Array of track data pointers\n\nTrack Data Entry:\nOffset | Size | Field Name     | Type | Description\n0x0    | 4    | dwDataSize     | int  | Size of track data (0 = no data)\n0x4    | 4    | pTrackData     | ptr  | Pointer to compressed track data",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "EXP",
      "index": "EXP:26",
