      "name": "ExecuteThreadCallback",
      "signature": "int ExecuteThreadCallback(CallbackParamBlock * pParamBlock)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Executes a thread callback function with specified parameters from a parameter block.\nThis function provides a safe mechanism for invoking callbacks stored in thread parameter \nblocks, commonly used in multi-threaded applications for deferred execution patterns.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load parameter block pointer from stack parameter\n2. Validate the parameter block contains a valid function pointer at offset 0x0  \n3. If function pointer is NULL, skip execution and return success (0)\n4. Extract first parameter (dwParam1) from offset 0x4 of parameter block\n5. Extract second parameter (dwParam2) from offset 0x8 of parameter block\n6. Push parameters onto stack in reverse order for call convention\n7. Call the function pointer with the two extracted parameters\n8. Return success status (0) regardless of callback execution result\n\nParameters:\npParamBlock (CallbackParamBlock *): Pointer to callback parameter structure containing:\n                                   - pfnCallback: Function pointer to execute (FARPROC)\n                                   - dwParam1: First parameter for callback (DWORD)  \n                                   - dwParam2: Second parameter for callback (DWORD)\n\nReturns:\n0: Always returns success, function does not propagate callback return values\n   Success indicates parameter block was processed, not callback success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL function pointer: Function returns success without executing callback\n- Invalid parameter block: No validation performed, may cause access violation\n- Callback exceptions: Not handled, will propagate to caller\n- Memory corruption: Parameter block dereferencing not protected\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type      Description\n0x00    4     pfnCallback   FARPROC   Function pointer to execute\n0x04    4     dwParam1      DWORD     First parameter for callback\n0x08    4     dwParam2      DWORD     Second parameter for callback",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
