      "name": "CleanupBinkFileHandle",
      "signature": "void CleanupBinkFileHandle(void * pBinkFile)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Safely cleanup and deallocate a Bink file handle structure\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pBinkFile pointer is not NULL to prevent crash\n2. Extract Windows file handle from offset 0xc in Bink structure  \n3. Call CloseHandle() to close the associated file descriptor\n4. Call RadFree() to deallocate the entire Bink structure memory\n5. Return void (no error handling - assumes cleanup always succeeds)\n\nParameters:\n- pBinkFile (void *): Pointer to BinkFileHandle structure to cleanup\n  IMPLICIT: None\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value (function always succeeds)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pointer: Function safely returns without action (null check protection)\n- Invalid handle: CloseHandle() and RadFree() handle invalid inputs gracefully\n\nStructure Layout (BinkFileHandle):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type      Description\n+0x00   ?     [unknown fields]  ?         Structure header/metadata  \n+0x0c   4     hFile            HANDLE    Windows file handle for cleanup\n[Additional fields unknown - structure size 132 bytes total]",
