      "name": "YuvInit",
      "signature": "void YuvInit(int nBitDepthMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize YUV-to-RGB color space conversion lookup tables and coefficients\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if core initialization flag (DAT_1003c80c) is clear, call FUN_1000b180() to initialize if needed\n2. Check if YUV tables flag (DAT_1003c81c) is clear, proceed with table generation if not initialized\n3. Generate YUV conversion coefficient lookup tables using fixed-point arithmetic\n   - Initialize coefficient arrays for Red (-0x811a80), Green (-0x662580), Blue (0x191280, 0x340780)\n   - Calculate normalized values using fixed-point division (>> 0xf) with rounding\n   - Populate global lookup tables for fast YUV-to-RGB conversion\n4. Initialize gamma correction and clipping tables (256 entries)\n   - Set base values and compute pointer offsets using coefficient indices\n   - Copy coefficient data to destination tables (0x800 = 2048 DWORDs)\n5. Set bit depth configuration based on input parameter (3-6 supported modes)\n   - Configure RGB bit masks and shift values for target pixel format\n   - Calculate bit field parameters: red/green/blue bit counts and shift amounts\n   - Store configuration in global coefficient storage areas\n6. Generate RGB conversion tables for 256-level luminance values\n   - Calculate RGB components using bit shifts and masks for target format\n   - Store both 16-bit and 32-bit packed pixel formats\n   - Handle luminance clamping and overflow to white (0xFFFFFF)\n\nParameters:\nnBitDepthMode (int): RGB bit depth configuration mode\n  - 3: 16-bit RGB (5-5-5 format with 10-bit total shift)\n  - 4: 16-bit RGB (5-6-5 format with 11-bit total shift) \n  - 5: 16-bit RGB (6-5-5 format with 11-bit total shift)\n  - 6: 16-bit RGB (6-6-4 format with 12-bit total shift)\n  - -1: Skip reconfiguration, use existing settings\n  - Other: Reset all coefficients to zero (invalid mode)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function modifies global lookup tables and configuration\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- First-time initialization: Sets up base coefficient tables (once per process)\n- Mode -1: Preserves current configuration for subsequent calls\n- Invalid modes: Zeros all coefficients, effectively disabling conversion\n- Luminance overflow: Values >= 0xDA25 (55845) map to maximum white\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x950A (38154): Fixed-point multiplier for YUV coefficient normalization\n0x7FFF (32767): Rounding mask for fixed-point arithmetic\n0x680F (26639): Red coefficient step increment per iteration\n0xCC4B (52299): Green coefficient step increment\n0x10235 (66101): Blue coefficient step increment  \n0x3225 (12837): Secondary coefficient decrement\n0xDB (219): Luminance scaling divisor\n0xDA25 (55845): Maximum luminance before white clipping\n0x10001 (65537): 16-bit duplication multiplier (copy low 16 bits to high 16)\n0xFFFFFF (16777215): Maximum RGB white value (24-bit)\n\nError Handling:\n- No explicit error checking - invalid bit modes result in zero coefficients\n- Global flags prevent double-initialization\n- Fixed-point arithmetic prevents floating point exceptions",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
