      "comment": "Processes table lookup operations for dual data streams using indexed value translation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize iteration counter with nIterationCount parameter\n2. Read byte index from first source pointer (DAT_100332e8)\n3. Advance first source pointer by 1 byte\n4. Lookup value from table (DAT_1003674c) using byte index as offset\n5. Store lookup value to current position of first destination pointer (DAT_100332e0)\n6. Store same lookup value to next position (DAT_100332e0 + 4)\n7. Read byte index from second source pointer (DAT_100332ec)\n8. Advance second source pointer by 1 byte\n9. Lookup value from same table using second byte index\n10. Store lookup value to current position of second destination pointer (DAT_100332e4)\n11. Store same lookup value to next position (DAT_100332e4 + 4)\n12. Advance both destination pointers by 8 bytes (2 x 4-byte values)\n13. Decrement iteration counter\n14. Repeat steps 2-13 until iteration counter reaches zero\n15. Return sum of nIterationCount and nReturnValue parameters\n\nParameters:\nnIterationCount (int): Number of lookup operations to perform (controls loop count)\nnReturnValue (int): Value to add to nIterationCount for return calculation\n\nReturns:\nSum of nIterationCount and nReturnValue parameters (nIterationCount + nReturnValue)\n\nGlobal Data Dependencies:\nDAT_100332e8 - First source data pointer (byte stream for table indices)\nDAT_100332ec - Second source data pointer (byte stream for table indices)\nDAT_100332e0 - First destination pointer (receives translated values)\nDAT_100332e4 - Second destination pointer (receives translated values)\nDAT_1003674c - Lookup table base address (256-entry table of 4-byte values)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction processes exactly nIterationCount iterations regardless of data content\nEach iteration consumes 1 byte from each source stream\nEach iteration produces 2 consecutive 4-byte values in each destination stream\nSource pointers are automatically advanced during processing\nDestination pointers are advanced by 8 bytes per iteration (stride = 2 * sizeof(int))\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x4 (4): Size of each table entry and destination value in bytes\n0x8 (8): Total advancement per destination pointer (2 values * 4 bytes each)",
