      "name": "CapturePerformanceTimestamp",
      "signature": "undefined8 CapturePerformanceTimestamp(undefined4 dwUnused, undefined4 dwHighTimestamp, undefined4 nStartValue, undefined4 nEndValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined8",
      "comment": "Captures high-precision performance timestamp using processor RDTSC instruction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read current processing counter state from global pointer\n2. Check if processing state is inactive (g_dwProcessingState == 0)\n3. Verify input parameters are different (nStartValue != nEndValue)\n4. Confirm performance timer is initialized (g_fPerformanceTimerInitialized == 1)\n5. Test processing counter bit 0 (uVar1 & 1) for timestamp capture readiness\n6. Set processing counter bit 2 (uVar1 | 4) to mark timestamp capture in progress\n7. Execute RDTSC instruction to capture 64-bit timestamp\n8. Store high 32 bits of timestamp in dwHighTimestamp parameter\n9. Store low 32 bits of timestamp in global g_dwRdtscLowValue (0x10036b4c)\n10. Test processing counter bit 1 (uVar1 & 2) for return path selection\n11. Return combined 64-bit value from dwHighTimestamp and selected input value\n\nParameters:\ndwUnused - Unused input parameter passed in ECX register\ndwHighTimestamp - Receives high 32 bits of RDTSC result, passed in EDX register\nnStartValue - Start comparison value, returned if bit 1 clear (stack parameter)\nnEndValue - End comparison value, returned if bit 1 set (stack parameter)\n\nReturns:\nCombined 64-bit value using CONCAT44(dwHighTimestamp, selected_value)\n- High 32 bits: dwHighTimestamp (from RDTSC or original parameter)\n- Low 32 bits: nEndValue if processing counter bit 1 set, otherwise nStartValue\n- Function returns undefined8 representing the combined timestamp/value pair\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_dwProcessingState != 0: skips timestamp capture, jumps to flag check\n- If nStartValue == nEndValue: skips timestamp capture, jumps to flag check\n- If g_fPerformanceTimerInitialized != 1: uses nStartValue, skips timestamp\n- If processing counter bit 0 set: skips RDTSC capture, jumps to flag check\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1 (bit 0) - Timestamp capture readiness flag\n0x2 (bit 1) - Return path selector flag  \n0x4 (bit 2) - Timestamp capture in progress marker\n0x10036b4c - Global storage for RDTSC low 32 bits (g_dwRdtscLowValue)\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error handling - function relies on global state validation\nPerformance timer must be initialized before calling this function\nInvalid processing state causes timestamp capture to be bypassed\n\nState Machine:\nState 1: Initial check \u2192 verify processing inactive and parameters differ\nState 2: Timer validation \u2192 confirm performance timer initialized\nState 3: Readiness test \u2192 check bit 0 for RDTSC capture permission\nState 4: Timestamp capture \u2192 execute RDTSC, store results, set bit 2\nState 5: Return selection \u2192 test bit 1 to choose nStartValue or nEndValue",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
