      "name": "ConvertBytesToPixels",
      "signature": "void ConvertBytesToPixels(void * pUnused, uint dwByteCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts grayscale byte values to 32-bit pixel format with color overlay.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if byte count is at least 2 (dwByteCount >= 2)\n2. Calculate loop iterations as half the byte count (processing pairs)\n3. For each pair of bytes from destination buffer:\n   a. Read first byte, replicate to R/G channels, add 0x800080\n   b. Write result to source buffer as 32-bit pixel\n   c. Read second byte, replicate similarly\n   d. Write second pixel, advance both buffer pointers\n4. Continue until all byte pairs processed\n\nParameters:\n- pUnused (void*): Unused parameter, likely for calling convention alignment\n- dwByteCount (uint): Number of bytes to convert (should be even)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x800080: Color overlay value (magenta component in RGB)\n- 0x10 (16): Bit shift for red channel positioning\n- 0x8 (8): Bit shift for green channel positioning",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:dc824d7f3cce9f70dfa5817d04987417",
