      "name": "ProcessYuvPixelConversion",
      "signature": "int ProcessYuvPixelConversion(int nPixelPairs, int nAdditionalValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Processes YUV pixel pairs into RGB format with pixel duplication for upscaling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter from pixel pairs parameter\n2. Read Y (luma) values from current destination buffer positions\n3. Read U and V (chroma) values from chroma buffers, advance chroma pointers\n4. Pack Y1, U, Y1, V into 32-bit YUV pixel (using CONCAT operations)\n5. Read second Y (luma) value from destination buffer + 1\n6. Apply 0xff00ff mask to isolate Y and V components\n7. Create RGB pixel by duplicating second Y value in high and low positions\n8. Combine with masked YUV components using bit shifts and OR operations\n9. Store both YUV and RGB pixels to current source buffer positions\n10. Store duplicated pixels to source buffer + stride offset for vertical duplication\n11. Process second set of pixels from end buffers using same conversion\n12. Store second pixel pair to end source buffer positions with stride offset\n13. Advance all buffer pointers: destination +2, source +2, chroma +1 each\n14. Decrement remaining pairs counter by 2, continue if > 0\n15. Return sum of original parameters\n\nParameters:\nnPixelPairs (int): Number of pixel pairs to process in loop iteration\nnAdditionalValue (int): Additional value added to first parameter in final result\n\nReturns:\nSum of nPixelPairs + nAdditionalValue\n\nSpecial Cases:\nLoop processes 2 pixel pairs per iteration, counter decrements by 2 each cycle\nChroma buffers advance by 1 while luma buffers advance by 2 (4:2:2 subsampling)\nPixel duplication creates 2x2 blocks from each source pixel pair\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xff00ff - Bit mask to isolate Y and V components, zeros out U component\n0x10 (16) - Left shift amount for high byte positioning in pixel packing\n0x8 (8) - Left shift amount for byte positioning in 32-bit pixel\n0x2 - Advancement step for luma/destination buffers (2 bytes per iteration)\n0x1 - Advancement step for chroma buffers (1 byte per U/V component)",
