      "name": "YuvBlit32bpp",
      "signature": "void YuvBlit32bpp(byte * pYPlane, byte * pUPlane, byte * pVPlane, dword dwYStride, dword dwUVStride, dword dwWidth, dword dwHeight, dword dwTargetStride, byte * pTargetBuffer, dword dwTargetPitch, dword dwFlags, dword dwPixelFormat)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Blits YUV planar video data to 32-bit RGB target buffer with format conversion.\nThis function acts as a stdcall wrapper around internal YUV converter function,\npassing all parameters plus a global mode flag for configuration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve all YUV plane parameters from stack (Y, U, V pointers and strides)\n2. Retrieve target buffer parameters (pointer, pitch, dimensions, format flags)  \n3. Push global mode flag pointer (g_dwYuvBlitMode) to stack as 13th parameter\n4. Call internal YUV conversion function FUN_1000bef0 with all parameters\n5. Clean up stack with 0x34 bytes (52 decimal = 13 parameters * 4 bytes)\n6. Return to caller with stdcall cleanup of 0x30 bytes (48 decimal = 12 parameters)\n\nParameters:\npYPlane - Pointer to Y (luminance) plane data buffer\npUPlane - Pointer to U (chrominance blue) plane data buffer\npVPlane - Pointer to V (chrominance red) plane data buffer  \ndwYStride - Bytes per row in Y plane\ndwUVStride - Bytes per row in U/V planes (usually half Y stride)\ndwWidth - Image width in pixels\ndwHeight - Image height in pixels\ndwTargetStride - Bytes per row in target buffer\npTargetBuffer - Pointer to 32-bit RGB output buffer\ndwTargetPitch - Target buffer pitch/stride (may differ from stride)\ndwFlags - Conversion flags and options for format control\ndwPixelFormat - Target pixel format specification (RGB ordering, etc.)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs blit operation without return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nGlobal mode flag g_dwYuvBlitMode (value 0x4) passed as additional parameter.\nFunction acts as stdcall wrapper around internal cdecl converter.\nStack cleanup handles both stdcall return (48 bytes) and internal call setup.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x34 (52 decimal) - Stack cleanup for internal call (13 parameters * 4 bytes)\n0x30 (48 decimal) - Stdcall return cleanup (12 parameters * 4 bytes)  \n0x4 - Current value in g_dwYuvBlitMode global variable",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "EXP",
      "index": "EXP:62",
