      "name": "TestCpuidSupport",
      "signature": "bool TestCpuidSupport(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Tests if the processor supports the CPUID instruction by checking ID flag modifiability.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save processor state by pushing all registers and segment registers\n2. Capture current EFLAGS register value into dwOriginalFlags\n3. Create modified flags by toggling ID bit (0x200000) -> dwModifiedFlags = dwOriginalFlags ^ 0x200000\n4. Attempt to load modified flags into EFLAGS register\n5. Read EFLAGS back to verify if ID bit change took effect\n6. Restore original EFLAGS to prevent side effects\n7. If ID bit toggle succeeded, processor supports CPUID instruction flag modification\n8. Execute CPUID instruction with function 1 to get processor features\n9. Check Feature Information EDX bit 23 (0x800000) for processor serial number support\n10. Return true if both ID flag modification and serial number feature supported\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\ntrue: Processor supports CPUID instruction with modifiable ID flag and serial number feature\nfalse: Processor lacks CPUID support or ID flag cannot be modified\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf ID flag modification fails (step 5), processor is older (386/early 486) without CPUID support\nCPUID function 1 returns processor feature flags in structured format\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x200000: ID flag bit position in EFLAGS register (bit 21)\n0x800000: Processor serial number support bit in CPUID EDX register (bit 23)\n0x1: CPUID function code for processor information and feature bits\n\nStructure Layout:\nCpuidResult layout (16 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name  Type  Description\n0x0     4     eax         uint  Main processor information\n0x4     4     ebx         uint  Additional feature information\n0x8     4     ecx         uint  Extended feature flags\n0xC     4     edx         uint  Standard feature flags (bit 23 = serial number support)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:8d5920c205e717477a0e065a3b217cfc",
