      "name": "ProcessYuvToRgbConversion",
      "signature": "int ProcessYuvToRgbConversion(int nLineWidth)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Processes YUV to RGB color space conversion using MMX instructions for two buffer regions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Calculate end pointer for current buffer region using line width parameter\n2. Initialize chroma buffer pointers (U and V components)\n3. Process first buffer region (current):\n   a. Load U and V chroma values from respective buffers\n   b. Load 64-bit packed pixel data from destination buffer\n   c. Advance chroma buffer pointers\n   d. Interleave U, V, and pixel data using CONCAT operations for RGB conversion\n   e. Store converted 8-byte result to source buffer current position\n   f. Advance destination buffer pointer by 2 positions\n   g. Store second 8-byte result with high-order pixel data to source buffer + 2\n   h. Advance source buffer pointer by 4 positions\n   i. Continue until reaching calculated end pointer\n4. Calculate end pointer for second buffer region using line width parameter\n5. Process second buffer region (end) using identical algorithm as step 3\n6. Return status value from EAX register\n\nParameters:\n\nnLineWidth (int): Width of scan line in pixels used to calculate buffer end positions\n\nReturns:\n\nnResultStatus (int): Processing status code from EAX register\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nMMX/SSE instruction usage for performance optimization in color conversion\nBuffer pointer arithmetic assumes 32-bit aligned pixel data\nTwo-pass processing for current and end buffer regions with identical algorithms\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x2: Destination buffer advance increment (2 x 32-bit values)\n0x4: Source buffer advance increment (4 x 32-bit values) \n-0x4: End pointer offset adjustment for line width calculation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
