      "name": "ConvertYuvToRgbPixelPairs",
      "signature": "void ConvertYuvToRgbPixelPairs(int nPixelPairCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts YUV color space pixel pairs to RGB format using lookup tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Cache initial chroma buffer pointers for restoration after first loop\n2. Process first loop: Read U/V chroma values, calculate lookup indices for Y->R, V->R, Y->G, U->B\n3. For each pixel pair in first iteration:\n   - Read Y luminance from destination buffer\n   - Calculate lookup table index from Y value\n   - Read two chroma pixels (U,V) and compute color components\n   - Combine R,G,B components using bitwise OR from lookup tables\n   - Store combined RGB values to source buffer\n   - Advance buffer pointers for next pixel pair\n4. Process second loop with restored chroma buffer positions:\n   - Read cached U/V chroma values from start positions\n   - Process remaining pixel pairs using same lookup methodology\n   - Calculate final R,G,B values and store to end buffer\n5. Restore chroma buffer pointers to original positions minus one\n\nParameters:\nnPixelPairCount: Number of pixel pairs to process (int)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nLoop processes pixels in pairs for chroma subsampling efficiency\nChroma buffers are shared between pixel pairs (4:2:0 sampling)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x4 - DWORD stride for lookup table indexing\nLookup table stride matches 32-bit integer array access pattern\n\nStructure Layout:\nGlobal buffers maintain separate Y, U, V color component data\n- g_pDstBufferCurrent/g_pDstBufferEnd: Y luminance data pointers\n- g_pChromaBufferU/g_pChromaBufferV: U/V chrominance data pointers  \n- g_pSrcBufferCurrent/g_pSrcBufferEnd: RGB output buffer pointers\n\nLookup Tables:\n- DAT_10030694: Red component lookup table (Y*index + offset)\n- DAT_1003bfc4: Green component lookup table (composite Y+U+V)\n- DAT_1003a3a0: Blue component lookup table (V*index + offset)  \n- DAT_10033320: Y luminance to lookup index conversion table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:83e334a5e7daaaacc1cfeb45b9bc65ce",
