      "comment": "Blend pixel data from source buffers into destination buffers using MMX SIMD instructions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load 64-bit MMX blend mask from g_qwMmxBlendMask into MM2 register\n2. Initialize source and destination buffer pointers from global variables  \n3. Phase 1: Process current buffer pair (g_pSrcBufferCurrent to g_pDstBufferCurrent)\n   a. Load 32-bit pixel data from destination buffer current position\n   b. Extract individual byte components from blend mask (bits 24, 16, 8, 0)\n   c. Load 32-bit pixel from destination buffer into MM1 register using MOVD\n   d. Unpack bytes to words using PUNPCKLBW MM1, MM2 for parallel processing\n   e. Store blended 64-bit result back to source buffer using MOVQ\n   f. Advance both pointers: source +8 bytes, destination +4 bytes\n   g. Continue until source pointer reaches (g_pSrcBufferCurrent + nPixelCount * 2)\n4. Update global pointers: g_pSrcBufferCurrent and g_pDstBufferCurrent \n5. Phase 2: Process end buffer pair (g_pSrcBufferEnd to g_pDstBufferEnd)\n   a. Repeat same blending operations as Phase 1\n   b. Continue until source pointer reaches (g_pSrcBufferEnd + nPixelCount * 2)\n6. Update final global pointer: g_pSrcBufferEnd\n\nParameters:\nnPixelCount (int): Number of pixels to process in each buffer pair\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function modifies global buffer pointers and writes blended data\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses MMX SIMD instructions for parallel byte processing (MOVD, PUNPCKLBW, MOVQ)\n- Processes two separate buffer pairs sequentially\n- Source buffers advance by 8 bytes (64-bit writes), destination by 4 bytes (32-bit reads)\n- Global buffer pointers are updated to reflect new positions after processing\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x8 - Source buffer stride (64-bit MMX register size)\n0x4 - Destination buffer stride (32-bit pixel size)  \n0x18 - Bit shift for alpha channel extraction (24 bits)\n0x10 - Bit shift for red channel extraction (16 bits)\n0x8 - Bit shift for green channel extraction (8 bits)\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\ng_qwMmxBlendMask at 0x1002dfe8 - 64-bit MMX blend mask\ng_pSrcBufferCurrent at 0x100332e0 - Current source buffer write pointer\ng_pDstBufferCurrent at 0x100332e8 - Current destination buffer read pointer\ng_pSrcBufferEnd at 0x100332e4 - End source buffer write pointer \ng_pDstBufferEnd at 0x100332ec - End destination buffer read pointer",
