      "name": "DecodeCoefficientsFromBitStream",
      "signature": "void DecodeCoefficientsFromBitStream(void * pOutputBlock, int * pBitStreamContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Decodes coefficients from a bit stream using variable-length encoding and multiple phases.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Extract initial bit depth from bit stream (4 bits) and validate against minimum threshold\n2. Initialize coefficient output arrays and processing stacks for dual-phase processing\n3. Zero-fill coefficient buffer array (31 uint values) for clean state\n4. Set up bit mask value (1 << (bitDepth - 1)) for sign bit extraction\n5. Phase 1: Process coefficient tree if bit depth > 1\n   a. Create nested loop structure for bit depth levels\n   b. Process stack entries using 4-state switch (0-3) based on low 2 bits\n   c. State 0: Add 0x11 offset to coefficient index\n   d. State 1: Generate 4 sequential entries (offset+0x02, 0x12, 0x22, 0x32)\n   e. State 2: Mark entry as processed (set to 0)\n   f. State 3: Extract multi-bit coefficient value with sign processing\n   g. Use bit manipulation for coefficient extraction and sign determination\n   h. Store signed coefficient values in auStack_114 array indexed by entry\n6. Phase 2: Final coefficient processing loop\n   a. Process remaining stack entries with simplified 4-state logic\n   b. Extract single-bit coefficients for states 0-2\n   c. State 3: Extract index and store +/-1 values based on bit state\n7. Update bit stream context with new position and remaining bits\n8. Copy processed coefficients to output structure at specific offsets\n   a. Copy 16-bit coefficient at offset 0x2\n   b. Copy 32-bit coefficients at offsets 0x4-0x7c (31 values total)\n\nParameters:\n\npOutputBlock (void *): Pointer to output coefficient structure receiving processed values\npBitStreamContext (int *): Pointer to 4-element context array [pData, nOffset, dwBitsValue, nBitsRemaining]\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - Updates output structure in-place and advances bit stream position\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nIf bit depth is 0 or 1, skips Phase 1 processing and only runs final phase\nHandles bit stream boundary crossings by fetching new 32-bit words as needed\nSign bit processing: coefficient |= mask, then negated if sign bit set\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x4: Minimum bit extraction size for initial processing\n0x1f: Bit mask for 5-bit values (31 decimal)\n0x11: Base offset for state 0 processing\n0x02, 0x12, 0x22, 0x32: Sequential offsets for state 1 quad generation\n0x3: Mask for extracting low 2 bits for state determination\n0x1c: Bit adjustment value (28 decimal) for stream alignment\n0x20: Constant for 32-bit calculations and shifts\n0xffffffff: Full bit mask for shift operations\n\nAlgorithm Verification:\n\nStep 1: Extract bit depth with (param_2[2] & 0xF) - extracts 4 bits from stream\nStep 2: Initialize stacks with local_40[6] and local_3a[58] arrays  \nStep 3: Zero coefficient array with REP STOSD for 31 iterations\nStep 4: Set mask = (1 << (bitDepth-1)) for sign bit isolation\nStep 5: Dual nested loops process coefficient tree by bit depth levels\nStep 6: Switch statement processes 4 encoding states per coefficient\nStep 7: Final phase extracts remaining coefficients with +/-1 values",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
