      "name": "DecompressBitStreamData",
      "signature": "void DecompressBitStreamData(uchar * pbOutputBuffer, BitStreamState * pBitStream, int nMaxOutputCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Decompress bit-stream encoded data using lookup table methodology.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output buffer to zero (clear 64 bytes)\n2. Extract initial bit position and buffer state from pBitStream\n3. Align bit stream if less than 3 bits available (refill from next word)\n4. Initialize lookup table with base values [0x10, 0x60, 0xb0, 0x02]\n5. Calculate bit mask from current bit position (1 << (bitPos & 7))\n6. For each bit position loop (bitPos & 7) + 1 iterations:\n   a. Process all pending array indices by reading bits and updating output\n   b. Process lookup table entries based on 2-bit encoding scheme:\n      - 00: Transform entry (value & 0xFC) + 0x11\n      - 01: Split into 4 new entries and advance end pointer\n      - 10: Mark entry as processed (set to 0) and advance\n      - 11: Add to pending array and write to output buffer\n   c. Handle bit refill when buffer exhausted\n   d. Terminate early if output count reaches nMaxOutputCount\n   e. Right-shift bit mask for next iteration\n7. Update pBitStream state with current position and remaining bits\n\nParameters:\npbOutputBuffer (uchar *): Target buffer for decompressed data\npBitStream (BitStreamState *): Bit stream state containing data pointer, bit buffer, and position\nnMaxOutputCount (int): Maximum number of bytes to decompress\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates pBitStream state and writes to pbOutputBuffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEarly termination when nOutputCount reaches nMaxOutputCount\nAutomatic bit buffer refill when exhausted (sets remaining bits to 0x1F)\nLookup table expansion from 4 to up to 67 entries during processing\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10, 0x60, 0xb0, 0x02: Initial lookup table values for decoding scheme\n0x1F (31): Bits per word minus 1 for refill operations  \n0x11, 0x12, 0x22, 0x32: Transformation constants for encoding types\n0x03: Bit mask for 2-bit encoding type extraction\n0x07: Bit mask for bit position within byte\n0xFC: Mask to clear lower 2 bits during transformation\n\nStructure Layout:\nBitStreamState (16 bytes):\nOffset Size Field Name    Type     Description\n+0x00    4   pData        uint *   Pointer to input data stream\n+0x04    4   nReserved    int      Reserved/unused field\n+0x08    4   dwBitBuffer  uint     Current buffered bits  \n+0x0C    4   dwBitCount   uint     Number of valid bits in buffer\n\nNote: Function uses 14 phantom stack variables optimized away by decompiler\nVariable names preserved from original analysis for debugging purposes",
