      "name": "BinkDirectSoundHandler",
      "signature": "void BinkDirectSoundHandler(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes a DirectSound audio context with the specified audio format parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear the DirectSound context structure (188 bytes) to initialize all fields to zero\n2. Initialize the base DirectSound interface by calling InitializeDirectSoundInterface()\n3. If DirectSound initialization fails, return 0 (failure)\n4. Store audio format parameters in context structure at specific offsets:\n   - Store bits per sample (nBitsPerSample) at context[0xd] and context[0x14]\n   - Store channel count (nChannels) at context[0xe] and context[0x15] \n   - Store sample rate (nSampleRate) at context[0x13] and context[0xc]\n5. Calculate audio format values:\n   - Extract lower 8 bits of channels for wChannelMask\n   - Calculate block alignment: (bits per sample >> 3) * channel count\n   - Calculate bytes per second: block alignment * sample rate\n6. Initialize DirectSound buffer if global DirectSound flag is set:\n   - Set up DirectSound buffer creation structure with size 0x14\n   - Call DirectSound interface CreateBuffer method\n   - If successful, configure buffer format and start playback\n   - Clear the global DirectSound initialization flag\n7. Calculate optimal buffer size based on audio quality setting:\n   - Use quality multiplier: 100ms for standard, 175ms for high quality (0x4b + 100)\n   - Calculate minimum buffer size in bytes\n   - Find next power of 2 that accommodates the minimum size\n8. Set buffer parameters in context structure:\n   - Set buffer segment count to 4 and multiplier to 1\n   - Double the multiplier until it exceeds calculated size\n   - Set final buffer size to multiplier * 4 bytes\n   - Calculate timing value: (multiplier * 3 * 1000) / bytes per second\n9. Create secondary DirectSound buffer with calculated parameters\n10. Set audio buffer size based on bit depth (double for 8-bit audio)\n11. Initialize volume controls to maximum (0x7fff)\n12. Call audio initialization functions FUN_1001c2c0() and FUN_1001c390()\n13. Initialize audio state variables and handles to default values\n14. Set up function pointer table with 8 audio callback functions\n15. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\npContext: Pointer to DirectSoundContext structure to initialize (188 bytes)\nnSampleRate: Audio sample rate in Hz (e.g., 22050, 44100)\nnBitsPerSample: Audio bit depth - 8 or 16 bits per sample\nnChannels: Number of audio channels (1=mono, 2=stereo)\n\nReturns:\n1: Success - DirectSound context initialized successfully\n0: Failure - DirectSound interface initialization failed or buffer creation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- For 8-bit audio (nBitsPerSample == 8), audio buffer size is doubled\n- High quality audio mode increases buffer size by 75% (175ms vs 100ms base)\n- Buffer size is always rounded up to next power of 2 for optimal performance\n- Timing calculations ensure smooth audio playback without gaps\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x2f (47): Number of DWORDs to clear (188 bytes / 4 = 47)\n0x4b (75): Additional milliseconds for high quality audio mode\n100: Base buffer duration in milliseconds for standard quality\n1000: Conversion factor for milliseconds to seconds\n0x7fff (32767): Maximum volume setting for audio channels\n0x180e0: DirectSound buffer creation flags (DSBCAPS_CTRLVOLUME | other flags)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type    Description\n0x00    32    pfnCallbacks[8]      void*   Function pointer table for audio operations  \n0x20    4     dwBufferSize         uint    Audio buffer size in bytes\n0x24    4     dwFlags              uint    Audio processing flags\n0x28    4     bInitialized         uint    Initialization status flag\n0x2c    4     dwTimingValue        uint    Timing calculation result\n0x30    4     dwParam1             uint    Sample rate parameter copy\n0x34    2     wBitsPerSample       ushort  Audio bit depth (8 or 16)\n0x38    4     dwSampleRate2        uint    Secondary sample rate storage\n0x50    4     dwBitsPerSample2     uint    Secondary bit depth storage\n0x54    4     dwChannels2          uint    Secondary channel count storage",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
