      "name": "ProcessAudioBufferWithWait",
      "signature": "void ProcessAudioBufferWithWait(BinkAudioContext * pAudioContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes audio buffer with retry logic until data is ready, then fills with silence pattern\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enter retry loop for audio buffer processing\n2. Set up parameters: buffer pointer, metadata buffers, context references\n3. Call virtual method at offset 0x2c (likely ProcessBuffer or GetBuffer)\n4. If result equals 0x88780096 (DSERR_BUFFERLOST), sleep 10ms and call reset method at offset 0x50\n5. Continue retry loop until different result code received\n6. On success (result == 0), verify bytes processed equals expected buffer size\n7. Calculate silence pattern based on audio bit depth (0x80 for 16-bit, 0x00 for 8-bit)\n8. Fill buffer with silence pattern using optimized 32-bit STOSD followed by byte cleanup\n9. Call completion method at offset 0x4c to finalize buffer processing\n\nParameters:\npAudioContext (BinkAudioContext *): Audio context containing interface pointer and buffer metadata\n- Offset 0x0: Virtual function table pointer\n- Offset 0x4: Buffer size or pointer to buffer\n- Offset 0x14: Audio format flags (0x10 indicates 16-bit audio)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Error code 0x88780096 (DSERR_BUFFERLOST): DirectSound buffer lost, triggers retry with reset\n- Non-zero result codes: Exit without processing (error conditions)\n- Buffer size mismatch: Exit without processing (sanity check failure)\n- 16-bit audio (flag 0x10): Fill with 0x80 silence pattern\n- 8-bit audio (not 0x10): Fill with 0x00 silence pattern\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x88780096: DSERR_BUFFERLOST DirectSound error code\n- 0x2c: Virtual method offset for buffer processing/acquisition\n- 0x50: Virtual method offset for buffer reset/recovery\n- 0x4c: Virtual method offset for buffer completion/submission\n- 0x10: Audio format flag indicating 16-bit samples\n- 0x80808080: 16-bit silence pattern (0x80 repeated in each byte)\n- 0x80: Single byte silence pattern for 16-bit audio\n- 10: Sleep duration in milliseconds during retry\n\nError Handling:\n- DSERR_BUFFERLOST: Automatic recovery with Sleep(10) + reset call\n- Non-zero results: Function exits early without buffer processing\n- Buffer validation: Ensures processed bytes match expected buffer size",
