      "name": "InvokeAudioVirtualMethod",
      "signature": "void InvokeAudioVirtualMethod(AudioCallParams * pCallParams)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Invokes a virtual audio method through an object's vtable with parameters extracted from a call parameter structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load audio object pointer from pCallParams->pAudioObject\n2. Access object's vtable through double indirection ([pAudioObject][0])\n3. Extract four audio parameters from parameter structure offsets 0x38, 0x3c, 0x40, 0x44\n4. Call virtual method at vtable offset 0x4c with object pointer and extracted parameters\n5. Return immediately after virtual method completes\n\nParameters:\npCallParams (AudioCallParams *): Pointer to parameter structure containing audio object and method parameters\n  - pAudioObject: Pointer to audio object containing vtable\n  - param1-param4: Four DWORD parameters passed to virtual method\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function does not return a value; delegates entirely to virtual method\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type    | Description\n-------|------|---------------|---------|----------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | pAudioObject  | void*   | Pointer to audio object with vtable\n0x04   | 56   | reserved1     | byte[56]| Reserved/padding space\n0x38   | 4    | param1        | uint    | First method parameter\n0x3C   | 4    | param2        | uint    | Second method parameter  \n0x40   | 4    | param3        | uint    | Third method parameter\n0x44   | 4    | param4        | uint    | Fourth method parameter\n\nVirtual Method Call:\nThe function calls the virtual method at vtable offset 0x4c (19th function in vtable).\nCall signature: method(pAudioObject, param2, param1, param4, param3)\nNote: Parameter order is reordered during the call (param2, param1, param4, param3).\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- No validation performed on pCallParams pointer\n- No null-checking of pAudioObject before vtable access\n- Virtual method call could potentially fail if vtable is corrupted\n- Function assumes AudioCallParams structure is properly initialized",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
