      "name": "FormatFloatAsExponentialWithMode",
      "signature": "void FormatFloatAsExponentialWithMode(double * pValue, char * szOutput, int nPrecision, int nFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Wrapper function that sets formatting mode flag before calling exponential float formatter.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set global formatting mode flag DAT_1003c8f0 to 1 (enables special formatting mode)\n2. Call FormatFloatAsExponential with all parameters to perform actual formatting\n3. Reset global formatting mode flag DAT_1003c8f0 to 0 (restores default mode)\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pValue - Pointer to double-precision floating-point value to format\n  pszOutput - Output buffer to receive formatted exponential notation string\n  nPrecision - Number of decimal places to display after decimal point\n  nFlags - Formatting flags (converted to boolean for uppercase 'E' vs lowercase 'e')\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value (output written to pszOutput buffer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Global flag DAT_1003c8f0 controls formatting behavior in FormatFloatAsExponential\n  - Flag value 1 enables cached formatting mode, 0 enables full parsing mode\n  - Function ensures flag is always reset even if FormatFloatAsExponential modifies it\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x1 (1) - Formatting mode flag value (enables cached mode)\n  0x0 (0) - Default mode flag value (enables full parsing mode)\n\nError Handling:\n  - No explicit error checking performed\n  - Relies on FormatFloatAsExponential for all validation and error handling\n  - Assumes valid input parameters and sufficient output buffer capacity",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
